WEBVTT

1
00:03:14.603 --> 00:03:16.211
Yes.

2
00:03:16.404 --> 00:03:18.275
No, it's Simoni.

3
00:03:18.397 --> 00:03:20.234
Oh, it's you.

4
00:03:20.827 --> 00:03:22.611
Nope.

5
00:03:22.716 --> 00:03:25.322
Nothing, but nothing. Dead calm.

6
00:03:26.262 --> 00:03:28.867
- Bless you!
- It's Lagrume?

7
00:03:29.374 --> 00:03:31.997
At the Sevigné newsstand?
O.K.

8
00:03:33.029 --> 00:03:36.437
If I hear anything about the killer,
I'll give you a call.

9
00:03:37.907 --> 00:03:40.652
- He's driving himself nuts with that
killer. - And driving us, too.

10
00:04:49.138 --> 00:04:50.956
Hot toddy.

11
00:04:51.779 --> 00:04:53.747
- Hello.
- Hello, Mme Juteaux.

12
00:04:53.843 --> 00:04:57.822
- You're running late.
- With this heavy weather, I fell asleep.

13
00:04:57.925 --> 00:04:59.436
Have a good evening.

14
00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:29.786
This is the police.

15
00:06:29.925 --> 00:06:31.589
Hello?

16
00:06:31.727 --> 00:06:33.750
Speak up. I'm listening.

17
00:06:33.889 --> 00:06:36.523
It's from Quai Celestins.
Yes, hello.

18
00:06:37.618 --> 00:06:41.361
<i>Tell M. Maigret that the Marais Killer
has claimed a new victim.</i>

19
00:06:41.713 --> 00:06:44.301
Really? Where?
Tell me where.

20
00:06:44.773 --> 00:06:45.875
Rue Rosiers.

21
00:06:46.065 --> 00:06:47.895
What number?

22
00:06:48.432 --> 00:06:52.202
What number on Rue Rosiers?
The woman killer has struck again.

23
00:06:52.341 --> 00:06:55.751
The passageway on Rue Rosiers.
Must be at number 68.

24
00:06:58.171 --> 00:06:59.587
Hello. Headquarters?

25
00:07:00.136 --> 00:07:02.715
<i>This is the central station
of the 4th district.</i>

26
00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:04.838
<i>A woman was just attacked
on Rue Rosiers.</i>

27
00:07:04.879 --> 00:07:06.123
- Dead?
- I suppose.

28
00:07:06.125 --> 00:07:09.336
<i>Apparently it's the Marais killer.
He doesn't usually miss.</i>

29
00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:10.541
Has your wagon left?

30
00:07:10.542 --> 00:07:12.027
It's leaving now.

31
00:07:12.552 --> 00:07:15.906
Hello? They also asked me to
notify Inspector Maigret.

32
00:07:16.157 --> 00:07:18.597
You'll take care of it?
Thanks.

33
00:07:20.659 --> 00:07:23.442
- Well?
- He must have slipped out via Rue Caron.

34
00:07:23.546 --> 00:07:25.681
No. No way.

35
00:07:25.785 --> 00:07:27.971
- I'd have seen him.
- Apparently not.

36
00:07:28.076 --> 00:07:30.208
I was watching at the corner
of Rue St. Antoine.

37
00:07:32.175 --> 00:07:34.291
This is where we lost him.

38
00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:37.076
You two, get back to Rue Rosiers.

39
00:07:38.046 --> 00:07:40.066
Don't you think we should
notify the Crime Squad?

40
00:07:40.166 --> 00:07:42.670
- There's no hurry.
- Still, this concerns Maigret.

41
00:07:42.741 --> 00:07:44.909
If someone's going to catch the guy,
it might as well be us.

42
00:07:44.970 --> 00:07:49.149
What more could Maigret do? And a Chief
Inspector must be fast asleep at this hour.

43
00:07:53.361 --> 00:07:54.410
But...

44
00:07:55.319 --> 00:07:57.872
- What are you doing here?
- This is my home.

45
00:07:57.977 --> 00:08:01.403
That's not an answer. And at this hour,
butcher shops are closed!

46
00:08:01.473 --> 00:08:04.393
And who's going to prepare my orders
for tomorrow morning?

47
00:08:04.470 --> 00:08:06.061
What's going on?

48
00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:13.003
- Who are you?
- I'm the concierge.

49
00:08:20.644 --> 00:08:23.809
- Where are you going?
- The crime scene? Want a ride?

50
00:08:23.984 --> 00:08:27.551
- Who notified you? - Got a call 5
minutes ago.  Get in if you want a ride.

51
00:08:27.629 --> 00:08:30.784
- The Crime Squad will be there soon.
- The Crime Squad?

52
00:08:32.245 --> 00:08:35.060
Since everyone has already been
notified...

53
00:08:36.074 --> 00:08:39.938
Same work as with the other three.
Two stab wounds to the chest.

54
00:08:40.428 --> 00:08:41.983
One would have been enough.

55
00:08:42.063 --> 00:08:45.542
But this time, he used a different tool.
He's no longer using an awl.

56
00:08:45.717 --> 00:08:47.081
The wounds are larger.

57
00:08:47.151 --> 00:08:51.120
- What time did she go out?
- At half past. I even mentioned it to her.

58
00:08:52.999 --> 00:08:56.129
- Marguerite Juteaux, musician.
- Violinist.

59
00:08:56.251 --> 00:08:58.050
What a terrible loss.

60
00:08:58.327 --> 00:09:00.093
- Is there a husband?
- Of course.

61
00:09:00.136 --> 00:09:04.840
Poor M. Juteaux must be playing cards like
every Saturday night, and he has no idea.

62
00:09:06.116 --> 00:09:08.231
And the little girl asleep upstairs.

63
00:09:08.328 --> 00:09:11.737
- Say, Lucas... Where is he playing?
- At Bar Bastille.

64
00:09:11.824 --> 00:09:15.224
- Go get M. Juteaux at Bar Bastille.
- You're not checking out the apartment?

65
00:09:15.294 --> 00:09:18.425
Later. There's a kid asleep there.
She'll wake up soon enough.

66
00:09:18.510 --> 00:09:20.696
- Leave someone to guard the front door.
- Yes.

67
00:09:21.046 --> 00:09:22.951
You were in the area but saw nothing?

68
00:09:23.004 --> 00:09:26.701
I was there all right.
I can't stop thinking about it.

69
00:09:26.859 --> 00:09:29.202
- He was right under my nose!
- Bravo.

70
00:09:29.315 --> 00:09:31.728
It's my fault, I know.
I stopped by the cafe just this once...

71
00:09:31.798 --> 00:09:35.452
- No one is blaming you.
- I am! Right under my nose...

72
00:09:40.868 --> 00:09:44.313
- You can see, her clothes are shredded.
- Yes. As usual.

73
00:09:46.332 --> 00:09:48.937
- She was...
- What?

74
00:09:49.304 --> 00:09:51.838
Not even. He just tears them apart
and leaves them.

75
00:09:51.970 --> 00:09:56.148
- You think rape would make things better?
- It might help us to understand them.

76
00:09:56.427 --> 00:09:59.190
- If I may...
- Careful! You're stepping in the sauce.

77
00:09:59.260 --> 00:10:00.721
If you may what?

78
00:10:00.790 --> 00:10:04.672
Alfonsi and I could go back to
Rue Turenne, where he disappeared.

79
00:10:04.742 --> 00:10:08.395
Oh, if you like.  After all, you know
your neighborhood best.

80
00:10:09.287 --> 00:10:12.050
Well, then. Question anyone you see.

81
00:10:12.356 --> 00:10:14.612
You might get something out of them.

82
00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:16.875
<i>La vie en rose</i>

83
00:10:23.829 --> 00:10:27.309
Well, well! Bravo.
You at least aren't wasting time.

84
00:10:31.077 --> 00:10:33.192
Here's the murder weapon.

85
00:10:34.311 --> 00:10:36.715
- You see?
- It's a butcher's knife.

86
00:10:36.855 --> 00:10:40.527
- And I think Alfonsi and I know its owner.
- Could very well be.

87
00:10:40.718 --> 00:10:44.915
- Good. Follow up without me. You have
free rein. - Thank you, sir.

88
00:11:17.757 --> 00:11:18.648
Lapointe.

89
00:11:20.248 --> 00:11:22.906
- What's this circus?
- Lagrume's raid.

90
00:11:26.909 --> 00:11:30.091
- Inspector.
- You're here? It's been a while.

91
00:11:41.550 --> 00:11:42.161
Your name is...

92
00:11:42.162 --> 00:11:43.841
Barberot, Emile.

93
00:11:43.919 --> 00:11:46.646
Butcher. 22, Rue Turenne.
It's the 10th time I've told you.

94
00:11:47.337 --> 00:11:49.680
And this?
Remind you of anything?

95
00:11:49.907 --> 00:11:51.079
Of course.

96
00:11:52.128 --> 00:11:53.946
- Is it yours?
- No.

97
00:11:54.488 --> 00:11:58.317
Be careful how you answer.
A woman was killed with this.

98
00:11:59.348 --> 00:12:01.936
- Was she deboned?
- Deboned?

99
00:12:02.433 --> 00:12:06.629
Well, yes. When you use a deboning knife,
it's to debone. Goes without saying, no?

100
00:12:10.138 --> 00:12:12.918
That still doesn't tell us what
you were doing in your shop at 9pm.

101
00:12:12.919 --> 00:12:15.330
I was preparing the orders
for tomorrow Sunday!

102
00:12:15.645 --> 00:12:18.268
Because some of us
have to work for a living.

103
00:12:18.870 --> 00:12:20.741
Got anything from the knife?

104
00:12:20.846 --> 00:12:24.291
It's an Augent, the biggest supplier
to butcher shops.

105
00:12:24.641 --> 00:12:27.613
Judging from the wear,
it was made a while ago.

106
00:12:27.849 --> 00:12:29.370
Not much else.

107
00:12:29.615 --> 00:12:33.339
Some faint greasy prints, probably
overlaid by a gloved hand.

108
00:12:34.231 --> 00:12:38.165
- I took three snapshots. But, you know...
- OK, thanks anyway.

109
00:12:39.659 --> 00:12:42.474
<i>This is awful. I'm getting really fed up.</i>

110
00:12:42.772 --> 00:12:46.286
<i>I get up at 6am. I won't spend the night
listening to the two of you.</i>

111
00:12:46.373 --> 00:12:48.575
You see the type, sir?

112
00:12:48.742 --> 00:12:52.029
- You think the knife is his?
- Hard to know. He won't say.

113
00:12:52.134 --> 00:12:54.740
Well, keep looking.
This butcher or another...

114
00:12:54.809 --> 00:12:57.589
I just want the knife's owner.
Up to you to find him.

115
00:12:57.660 --> 00:12:59.443
You really think that...

116
00:12:59.531 --> 00:13:01.768
You found the lead.
It's yours.

117
00:13:02.101 --> 00:13:04.286
Rest assured I'll do my best, sir.

118
00:13:04.391 --> 00:13:06.471
I don't doubt it for a moment.

119
00:13:07.327 --> 00:13:09.075
Say, Lagrume...

120
00:13:09.452 --> 00:13:11.042
Thanks for calling me in.

121
00:13:11.146 --> 00:13:12.948
5 min. after the crime.
Can't do better.

122
00:13:13.559 --> 00:13:16.374
But I wasn't the one
who called you, sir.

123
00:13:19.573 --> 00:13:20.622
Alfonsi.

124
00:13:21.491 --> 00:13:22.540
Thank you.

125
00:13:24.044 --> 00:13:27.330
- For what? - For notifying me.
He doesn't always remember to do it.

126
00:13:27.470 --> 00:13:31.055
But I didn't do it either, sir.
A patrolman probably did.

127
00:13:33.726 --> 00:13:35.282
Yes, probably.

128
00:14:54.455 --> 00:14:57.236
- What are you looking for?
- The coffee pot.

129
00:15:01.439 --> 00:15:02.645
Cold or hot?

130
00:15:03.065 --> 00:15:04.202
Ah! Hot.

131
00:15:16.741 --> 00:15:18.560
Did you turn on the water?

132
00:15:29.668 --> 00:15:32.168
You have problems?
What's the matter?

133
00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:34.406
He's back at it.

134
00:15:36.259 --> 00:15:37.850
Another woman?

135
00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:41.811
And nothing?

136
00:15:42.388 --> 00:15:43.525
Nothing...

137
00:15:44.346 --> 00:15:46.706
A kid who's probably waking up now,

138
00:15:46.803 --> 00:15:50.064
a husband who doesn't understand,
and a creep who's off to sleep.

139
00:15:50.112 --> 00:15:51.720
That's all we have.

140
00:15:52.325 --> 00:15:55.647
We've questioned dozens of guys,
even a butcher.

141
00:15:56.417 --> 00:15:58.340
But I think he's innocent.

142
00:15:59.695 --> 00:16:02.317
Unless I got it wrong.
It's possible.

143
00:16:02.422 --> 00:16:06.286
After all, maybe it isn't only coffee pots
I've lost the knack for finding.

144
00:16:06.392 --> 00:16:07.423
Here.

145
00:16:09.267 --> 00:16:13.392
Don't worry about the suitcases.
I'm used to packing and unpacking.

146
00:16:14.337 --> 00:16:17.344
You'd better unpack the suitcases
once and for all.

147
00:16:17.457 --> 00:16:20.955
We could fix up the little house at
La Rochelle. I could putter around there.

148
00:16:21.060 --> 00:16:23.175
- You?
- I'm tired, Louise.

149
00:16:24.066 --> 00:16:25.063
Tired.

150
00:16:25.169 --> 00:16:27.651
For example, I'm losing my memory.

151
00:16:27.903 --> 00:16:30.509
Earlier, Alfonsi told me that...

152
00:16:31.400 --> 00:16:33.691
I don't even remember what he told me.

153
00:16:33.761 --> 00:16:34.845
Anyway...

154
00:16:35.212 --> 00:16:39.058
I thought I was on to something, and...
No, I swear, it feels like retirement.

155
00:16:39.329 --> 00:16:41.427
Well, then, let's retire.

156
00:16:42.048 --> 00:16:44.864
I know at least one person
who'll be happy about it.

157
00:16:44.934 --> 00:16:46.489
Your creep.

158
00:16:46.849 --> 00:16:48.623
You have to admit it's a success:

159
00:16:48.711 --> 00:16:51.613
Four murders in the 4th district,
and old Maigret goes fishing.

160
00:16:52.391 --> 00:16:55.722
He probably already had
a high opinion of himself. But now...

161
00:16:55.809 --> 00:16:58.484
It's simple. He only needs to
start killing every day.

162
00:16:58.563 --> 00:17:02.392
Why hold back if it's working?
Soon, he'll be giving interviews.

163
00:17:02.549 --> 00:17:04.809
Here. They're ready to crown him.

164
00:17:04.897 --> 00:17:09.573
<i>FROM JACK THE RIPPER TO MR. X
What Will the Killer Dare Next?
Inspector Maigret starts over again.</i>

165
00:17:09.644 --> 00:17:11.767
- He must be thinking: I'm the king.
- You believe he really thinks that way?

166
00:17:11.834 --> 00:17:13.074
I have no idea.

167
00:17:13.184 --> 00:17:16.488
But if he's at all proud,
he must be pleased with himself.

168
00:17:17.555 --> 00:17:20.300
- Proud...
- Why wouldn't he be?

169
00:17:30.693 --> 00:17:34.400
Hello, police? This is Inspector Maigret.
Give me headquarters.

170
00:17:37.145 --> 00:17:38.771
Headquarters?
Maigret.

171
00:17:39.750 --> 00:17:41.778
Who asked you to call me last night?

172
00:17:41.866 --> 00:17:43.596
The 4th district station.

173
00:17:43.648 --> 00:17:45.852
- <i>Can you put them on?</i>
- Easy.

174
00:17:47.661 --> 00:17:50.267
Please connect the 4th district
to Inspector Maigret.

175
00:17:55.538 --> 00:17:56.989
Hello. The 4th?

176
00:17:57.374 --> 00:17:59.298
It's about last night's call.

177
00:17:59.533 --> 00:18:01.789
I just passed on the message, sir.

178
00:18:02.794 --> 00:18:05.731
The call came from Box 28,
on Quai Celestins.

179
00:18:06.675 --> 00:18:09.700
No, not a watchman. The glass
was broken. A witness, probably.

180
00:18:10.207 --> 00:18:12.865
A witness, 600 meters
from the crime scene?

181
00:18:13.403 --> 00:18:16.550
I'd love to know what
your "witness" had to say.

182
00:18:16.970 --> 00:18:18.455
Yes, every word.

183
00:18:18.578 --> 00:18:19.592
He said:

184
00:18:20.274 --> 00:18:24.015
"You can notify M. Maigret that
the Marais Killer

185
00:18:24.131 --> 00:18:26.247
"has claimed a new victim."
That's all.

186
00:18:26.352 --> 00:18:28.205
OK, that's good.
Thanks.

187
00:18:35.560 --> 00:18:37.143
Say, there's a big brain

188
00:18:37.222 --> 00:18:38.375
under those rollers!

189
00:18:38.524 --> 00:18:40.937
You were right.
He's gloating.

190
00:18:41.086 --> 00:18:43.935
5 minutes after the crime,
he had the nerve to call me.

191
00:18:44.066 --> 00:18:45.325
"<i>Monsieur</i> Maigret."

192
00:18:45.832 --> 00:18:47.737
I'll show him "<i>Monsieur</i> Maigret!"

193
00:18:59.278 --> 00:19:01.149
- Hey, what...?
- Out of the way!

194
00:19:01.219 --> 00:19:03.754
- Is this for Maigret?
- You'll see. Let us through.

195
00:19:03.789 --> 00:19:06.219
- Is he a suspect? - A witness?
- All right, all right.

196
00:19:06.272 --> 00:19:09.698
- I can't say anything.
- Thanks for the cooperation!

197
00:19:11.026 --> 00:19:14.751
- If Lucas is here, it's for Maigret.
- If Lagrume is here, it's about the 4th.

198
00:19:14.820 --> 00:19:18.736
- The 4th, that's the Marais!
- Yes. Try to develop those right away.

199
00:19:18.850 --> 00:19:22.290
- Could be 5 columns if it's the killer!
- Could be a common thief.

200
00:19:22.377 --> 00:19:23.916
And that? That's a patrolman?

201
00:19:24.763 --> 00:19:27.316
- May I ask a quick question, sir?
- Sorry.

202
00:19:27.405 --> 00:19:30.797
- Just a little hint, Commissioner Guimard.
- Not right now.

203
00:19:31.409 --> 00:19:33.455
Is it the Marais Killer?

204
00:19:33.857 --> 00:19:36.375
I have no statement to make, Miss.

205
00:19:39.372 --> 00:19:41.479
They're all in there.
The game's afoot.

206
00:19:41.550 --> 00:19:44.793
I just hope he confesses
before the 5 o'clock edition.

207
00:19:48.334 --> 00:19:51.516
So, Mazet, here you are
on the other side of the gates.

208
00:19:52.031 --> 00:19:55.310
- Not too disoriented?
- Always happy to help out, sir.

209
00:19:55.381 --> 00:19:59.280
- And I hear that one good turn deserves
another. - Hey, not so fast.

210
00:19:59.384 --> 00:20:03.196
This isn't about your typical bank job.
It's about passing as a killer.

211
00:20:03.292 --> 00:20:06.229
Oh, I got the picture, sir.
I can even improve on it.

212
00:20:06.281 --> 00:20:08.345
Not too much. Not too much.

213
00:20:08.440 --> 00:20:12.199
Just tell me how you want your scoundrel.
Quivering or impudent?

214
00:20:12.733 --> 00:20:16.859
I seem to remember you played a pretty
good trick on us after your last bank job.

215
00:20:18.346 --> 00:20:20.426
I don't remember anymore.

216
00:20:20.924 --> 00:20:24.054
No one remembers anymore.
Am I right, sir?

217
00:20:24.264 --> 00:20:28.180
Stop with the blackmail, and listen.
I need a suspect, not a clown.

218
00:20:28.887 --> 00:20:33.067
I want you to give something plausible
and low-key to the journalists outside.

219
00:20:33.398 --> 00:20:36.808
- But after all, I killed 4 women!
- Even better reason not to wear a sign.

220
00:20:37.482 --> 00:20:41.135
The Paris-Presse guy is a 20 year veteran.
And little Rougin is full of trickery.

221
00:20:41.257 --> 00:20:43.373
They'll sniff it out if you overdo it.

222
00:20:43.451 --> 00:20:47.140
- What if they ask me questions? - You tell
them you're innocent and wrongly arrested.

223
00:20:47.215 --> 00:20:50.309
I want something classic.
Okay, take him to holding.

224
00:20:50.379 --> 00:20:53.535
- Oh, not holding!
- You'd prefer the state pen?

225
00:20:54.094 --> 00:20:56.228
No. No cuffs.
Go ahead.

226
00:21:00.494 --> 00:21:01.560
Gentlemen.

227
00:21:02.627 --> 00:21:03.816
Here he is!

228
00:21:04.428 --> 00:21:06.999
- Did he confess?
- Ask the Inspector.

229
00:21:11.890 --> 00:21:15.639
Note that the judge was very fair,
very understanding, but...

230
00:21:16.164 --> 00:21:18.420
- ... how shall I put it?
- not very hot.

231
00:21:18.579 --> 00:21:19.645
Not very.

232
00:21:20.449 --> 00:21:22.250
- And you?
- Lukewarm.

233
00:21:23.413 --> 00:21:24.951
Playing with the press...

234
00:21:25.021 --> 00:21:29.078
Giving it a fake killer in the hopes
of tweaking the real one's self-esteem...

235
00:21:29.182 --> 00:21:32.749
Sure. You'd prefer a clean investigation,
complete with supporting evidence.

236
00:21:32.827 --> 00:21:34.157
As would I.

237
00:21:34.611 --> 00:21:36.062
But I got nothing!

238
00:21:36.110 --> 00:21:38.714
I know we have no choice.
Still...

239
00:21:39.012 --> 00:21:42.544
To deploy almost 500 men...
To blanket an entire Paris neighborhood...

240
00:21:42.683 --> 00:21:45.219
And for how long?
If we only knew that...

241
00:21:45.315 --> 00:21:47.518
You must admit
those are huge responsibilities!

242
00:21:47.624 --> 00:21:52.650
- I'm putting you in a tough spot. I know.
- We're both in it. That's not the issue.

243
00:21:54.018 --> 00:21:54.612
Jules.

244
00:21:55.434 --> 00:21:57.322
Are you sure of your plan?

245
00:21:57.742 --> 00:21:58.808
I wish.

246
00:22:00.854 --> 00:22:04.963
What I'm sure of is that this bastard
went to the trouble of having me called.

247
00:22:05.102 --> 00:22:07.236
He's proud of himself and of his crimes.

248
00:22:07.288 --> 00:22:08.460
He's a showboat.

249
00:22:08.591 --> 00:22:12.507
If the papers say someone else is getting
credit for his deeds, he might get irked

250
00:22:12.603 --> 00:22:15.086
and try anything to restate his claim,

251
00:22:15.173 --> 00:22:16.467
to prove us wrong.

252
00:22:16.581 --> 00:22:18.382
To commit another crime.

253
00:22:18.469 --> 00:22:20.253
An anticipated attempt.

254
00:22:20.569 --> 00:22:24.731
We're playing on his ground. But we get
to provide the bait. And the trap.

255
00:22:24.835 --> 00:22:27.710
Algaron will send you
15 police secretaries.

256
00:22:27.973 --> 00:22:30.998
- It won't be easy for him.
- Put yourself in his shoes.

257
00:22:31.094 --> 00:22:33.751
You're not inviting these girls
to a party.

258
00:22:34.004 --> 00:22:37.099
To be honest, Camille, I've never
found myself so short on ideas.

259
00:22:37.161 --> 00:22:39.206
But I'm in a hurry.
A big hurry.

260
00:22:39.293 --> 00:22:43.000
Since May 1st, when he killed for the
first time, this guy has struck June 20th,

261
00:22:43.088 --> 00:22:45.011
July 10th and August 2nd.

262
00:22:45.124 --> 00:22:47.047
He acts in fits.
And the fits are getting closer.

263
00:22:47.144 --> 00:22:49.784
If we wait, we'll be on daily alert.
So...

264
00:22:49.872 --> 00:22:52.844
A proper investigation, you see...
This is about hunting a tiger.

265
00:22:54.023 --> 00:22:55.562
You know the principle.

266
00:22:55.693 --> 00:22:58.281
We tie a goat to a pole,
and we wait.

267
00:22:58.787 --> 00:23:00.519
Here, you're the goats.

268
00:23:00.694 --> 00:23:02.565
We were chosen for the resemblance?

269
00:23:03.369 --> 00:23:04.890
In a way, yes.

270
00:23:05.091 --> 00:23:07.329
Your resemblance to the victims.

271
00:23:07.923 --> 00:23:11.385
All 4 were brunettes, full figured
and not very tall.

272
00:23:12.784 --> 00:23:15.145
That's exactly the kind of woman
he must long

273
00:23:15.146 --> 00:23:15.896
to kill.

274
00:23:17.522 --> 00:23:20.556
That's why, my dears, you still have
the option of bowing out.

275
00:23:20.670 --> 00:23:22.348
What will we have to do?

276
00:23:22.461 --> 00:23:26.832
Well... Stroll, walk the neighborhood, look
like you're going to or coming from home.

277
00:23:27.604 --> 00:23:30.419
All the crimes took place
in the streets, at sunset.

278
00:23:30.540 --> 00:23:33.950
The last victim was headed to work.
The first two were coming from it.

279
00:23:34.055 --> 00:23:38.189
And the third was... well, in the middle
of doing it. So you have some options.

280
00:23:39.841 --> 00:23:42.867
She's wondering if we need to
hail the passers-by.

281
00:23:42.989 --> 00:23:45.708
Neither hail the passers-by,
nor speak to anyone.

282
00:23:45.795 --> 00:23:48.803
No one can know. No one.
Not even your families.

283
00:23:48.898 --> 00:23:50.594
Even in case of death?

284
00:23:50.699 --> 00:23:54.843
My dears, this is no joke. This guy has
killed 4 times, and killed ugly. So...

285
00:23:55.000 --> 00:23:56.609
You, come over here.

286
00:23:57.316 --> 00:24:00.559
Now, one of you. Anyone. You.
Step forward.

287
00:24:00.875 --> 00:24:04.424
Now, watch carefully. He always goes
about it the same way. Start walking.

288
00:24:04.649 --> 00:24:05.698
Go ahead.

289
00:24:07.169 --> 00:24:08.376
Look at me...

290
00:24:11.398 --> 00:24:14.371
- Hey, she took me by surprise!
- She wasn't looking.

291
00:24:14.991 --> 00:24:16.757
So, it's easy, eh?

292
00:24:17.246 --> 00:24:20.778
Should things not go so well,
start by screaming out loud.

293
00:24:20.865 --> 00:24:24.878
I'm not asking you to arrest him, but to
alert us. Whistles are made for that.

294
00:24:24.984 --> 00:24:27.116
There'll be plainclothesmen
hidden all over.

295
00:24:27.539 --> 00:24:28.868
So we can rest easy.

296
00:24:28.990 --> 00:24:30.004
Well, not I.

297
00:24:30.101 --> 00:24:34.227
You must keep in mind that the game
we're hunting is no ordinary prey.

298
00:24:34.326 --> 00:24:36.477
Outside of his fits,
he may be a regular guy.

299
00:24:36.547 --> 00:24:39.222
Suddenly, something goes off,
and he <i>needs</i> to kill.

300
00:24:39.327 --> 00:24:42.072
At that moment, he's capable
of attacking anyone, anyhow.

301
00:24:42.159 --> 00:24:45.027
In fact, I'm counting on that.
That's why you're here.

302
00:24:45.788 --> 00:24:48.568
- What? Is something unclear?
- So, in the paper...

303
00:24:48.569 --> 00:24:50.019
what's with the "madman?"

304
00:24:50.141 --> 00:24:51.943
That?
That's the trigger.

305
00:24:52.099 --> 00:24:53.323
Flabbergasting!

306
00:24:53.944 --> 00:24:56.304
I don't know
what the District Attorney will think.

307
00:24:56.410 --> 00:24:59.050
But I find the whole thing
flabbergasting.

308
00:24:59.286 --> 00:25:02.730
It is understood that you're taking
complete responsibility for this.

309
00:25:02.905 --> 00:25:04.715
Agreed entirely, your honor.

310
00:25:04.959 --> 00:25:08.324
I only took this responsibility
to relieve you of yours, sir.

311
00:25:09.758 --> 00:25:10.755
Of course!

312
00:25:10.851 --> 00:25:14.278
Well, my friend, in that case,
I can only wish you success.

313
00:25:14.704 --> 00:25:19.154
I do admit you chose your man well.
(<i>FACE OF A MADMAN?</i>)
You're sure he's innocent?

314
00:25:19.389 --> 00:25:22.118
That's something he and I don't
completely agree on.

315
00:25:23.899 --> 00:25:27.335
Very well, your honor.
My respects to Mme Coméliau.

316
00:25:28.609 --> 00:25:29.833
A madman...

317
00:25:30.339 --> 00:25:32.822
Well, take a bow.
You can be proud.

318
00:25:32.980 --> 00:25:35.480
You couldn't resist.
Had to have your little fit.

319
00:25:35.532 --> 00:25:39.440
You just had to do your number
and ham it up! You, clown, you!

320
00:25:39.588 --> 00:25:41.198
It was the pressure!

321
00:25:41.442 --> 00:25:44.869
- If I'd had time to rehearse...
- Oh, trust me, you'll get the time...

322
00:25:44.939 --> 00:25:47.474
In the hole, you hear?
You're going to the hole.

323
00:25:47.562 --> 00:25:50.429
You like entertainment?  We'll
make sure you're entertained.

324
00:25:50.526 --> 00:25:52.710
Take him away!
I don't want to see him.

325
00:25:52.806 --> 00:25:54.817
- Wow, they're getting vicious.
- Who?

326
00:25:54.922 --> 00:25:58.226
Anonymous letters.
You can now send them via air tube.

327
00:25:58.366 --> 00:25:59.940
And personal, too.

328
00:26:01.941 --> 00:26:06.413
<i>NO, M. Maigret. The killer of those sluts
in the Marais is not A MADMAN!</i>

329
00:26:08.520 --> 00:26:09.464
One moment.

330
00:26:12.070 --> 00:26:15.269
On second thought,
your little number isn't so bad.

331
00:26:15.426 --> 00:26:18.661
In any case, it seems to be working.
So keep it up.

332
00:26:18.809 --> 00:26:20.172
I'm telling you.

333
00:26:20.260 --> 00:26:23.600
- So we're not taking him away?
- Yes, and through the front door.

334
00:26:23.687 --> 00:26:25.121
And with cuffs on.

335
00:26:25.435 --> 00:26:29.107
- Are you sure we're okay?
- But hey, not too much!

336
00:26:30.261 --> 00:26:31.344
Just a bit.

337
00:26:31.668 --> 00:26:32.717
Go on.

338
00:26:35.523 --> 00:26:36.695
Here he is!

339
00:26:38.609 --> 00:26:41.127
- Clear out!
- Detective Torrence, is it the jackpot?

340
00:26:41.196 --> 00:26:44.799
- Is it true he's a madman?
- Read about it in the papers.

341
00:26:44.903 --> 00:26:47.229
With bracelets on, guys.
Smells like a charge.

342
00:26:50.922 --> 00:26:54.524
Won't you please give us some kind
of statement, Inspector?

343
00:26:56.229 --> 00:26:58.642
Just answer yes or no.
Is it him?

344
00:27:00.145 --> 00:27:01.719
After the reconstruction.

345
00:27:01.789 --> 00:27:04.831
- The reconstruction? What reconstruction?
- But where?

346
00:27:04.901 --> 00:27:05.950
When?

347
00:27:08.450 --> 00:27:10.356
- The reconstruction?
- Yes.

348
00:27:10.426 --> 00:27:12.786
When I get a letter,
I always answer.

349
00:27:12.909 --> 00:27:16.790
"No, <i>Monsieur</i> Maigret. The killer of those
sluts in the Marais is not a madman."

350
00:27:16.868 --> 00:27:20.172
- Think it's him? - It's his style. He's
already given me the "<i>Monsieur</i> Maigret."

351
00:27:20.688 --> 00:27:24.132
If he'll bother to write, maybe
this time, he'll bother to show up.

352
00:27:24.237 --> 00:27:28.364
The reconstruction will take place at 10
tomorrow night. That's my answer.

353
00:27:28.521 --> 00:27:31.205
And I'd like it mentioned
in tonight's papers.

354
00:27:31.292 --> 00:27:33.705
Nice work you have me doing.

355
00:27:34.693 --> 00:27:38.050
We're eating early tonight because of
the reconstruction. Will you be there?

356
00:27:38.152 --> 00:27:41.421
We would have gladly gone if
we didn't have tickets to a show.

357
00:27:41.475 --> 00:27:45.452
- Anyway, now that we know it's all over.
- Over? Ha! Only according to the police.

358
00:27:45.531 --> 00:27:49.330
Ah, I see you're like my husband.
He thinks the police are all liars.

359
00:27:49.434 --> 00:27:52.012
Liars? More like scum. Real scum.

360
00:27:52.253 --> 00:27:55.898
I'm a tax payer year round, and by way
of thanks, I get beat  up on holidays.

361
00:27:56.091 --> 00:27:59.640
- And what can I get for the gentleman?
- A small steak.

362
00:28:08.376 --> 00:28:09.881
Is this yours?

363
00:28:10.245 --> 00:28:11.993
Looks like it.
May I?

364
00:28:13.751 --> 00:28:15.744
Wow. My Augent!

365
00:28:16.915 --> 00:28:20.587
We really looked for it. Right, Gilberte?
I even thought it was stolen.

366
00:28:20.657 --> 00:28:23.716
- Where did you find it?
- We'll talk about it.

367
00:28:23.839 --> 00:28:26.987
But not here.
About that, and other things.

368
00:28:27.817 --> 00:28:29.356
Please come with me.

369
00:28:30.666 --> 00:28:35.195
Insulting an officer of the law! No one
likes cops, man! It's just a fact of life.

370
00:28:35.317 --> 00:28:38.726
- We can't arrest people for that!
- I meant well, sir.

371
00:28:38.953 --> 00:28:41.960
- And there was the knife.
- Then you should have called me.

372
00:28:42.057 --> 00:28:45.885
Imagine if the butcher blabs to the press.
My plan would be in shambles.

373
00:28:46.366 --> 00:28:48.884
So you and your initiatives. Thanks!

374
00:28:49.014 --> 00:28:52.143
- I'll make a note of it, sir.
- Stop right here.

375
00:28:52.363 --> 00:28:55.598
No point in being seen together.
Need I remind you of my orders?

376
00:28:55.737 --> 00:28:58.185
Go to the reconstruction site,
play onlooker,

377
00:28:58.324 --> 00:29:01.384
choose a random spectator and
follow him wherever he goes.

378
00:29:01.489 --> 00:29:03.605
- Any rookie can do it.
- No!

379
00:29:03.753 --> 00:29:06.760
In fact, 20 of your most experienced
colleagues will be doing the same.

380
00:29:06.883 --> 00:29:09.155
I want the names and addresses
of all present.

381
00:29:09.226 --> 00:29:11.727
With a little luck, you could be
the one to find him.

382
00:29:11.866 --> 00:29:13.475
- A little luck...
- Yes.

383
00:29:15.005 --> 00:29:16.544
Go on. See you soon.

384
00:29:16.910 --> 00:29:19.621
And lose this habit of
feeling like a target.

385
00:30:07.230 --> 00:30:09.722
Stop pushing! There'll be enough
for everyone.

386
00:30:10.123 --> 00:30:12.711
True, it's always the latecomers who...

387
00:32:44.449 --> 00:32:46.880
Step away, ladies and gentlemen.
Move along.

388
00:32:47.020 --> 00:32:49.406
- Are you hurt?
- No. Just scared.

389
00:32:49.493 --> 00:32:51.137
- And this?
- A scratch.

390
00:32:51.280 --> 00:32:53.064
- You saw him?
- No.

391
00:32:53.297 --> 00:32:57.335
I really tried to hang on. But he fought
back, and I couldn't hold on.

392
00:32:58.053 --> 00:33:01.129
Here. I found myself with this.
That's all.

393
00:33:02.939 --> 00:33:04.933
Come on. That's not so bad.

394
00:33:05.465 --> 00:33:07.808
That's impossible.
Everyone saw him run away.

395
00:33:07.878 --> 00:33:12.040
Everyone, everyone... It was impossible
last time too! And yet, nothing!

396
00:33:12.152 --> 00:33:14.425
- I was on Rue Caron.
- Both of us, chief.

397
00:33:14.505 --> 00:33:16.323
My God, he didn't fly away!

398
00:33:16.445 --> 00:33:19.295
If he came from here and he didn't come
out there, he must be in here!

399
00:33:19.400 --> 00:33:22.056
Cordon off this block and search it!

400
00:33:33.225 --> 00:33:35.726
- Are you the concierge?
- Here we go again.

401
00:33:35.857 --> 00:33:38.427
- I asked if you were the concierge.
- Of course I am!

402
00:33:38.531 --> 00:33:40.105
What time did you close the gate?

403
00:33:40.183 --> 00:33:44.502
I stayed outside with my neighbor from
No. 26, until about 15 minutes ago.

404
00:33:44.743 --> 00:33:47.698
- And no one has rung since?
- No, no one.

405
00:33:48.886 --> 00:33:52.549
Okay, you, search every floor from
the ground to the attic. On the double!

406
00:33:53.834 --> 00:33:56.754
Mind the feet! They're going to
muddy up my stairs again.

407
00:33:56.911 --> 00:33:59.481
You two, take care of the cellar.

408
00:34:01.886 --> 00:34:05.635
- Just between us, who did your vampire
kill this time? - No one.

409
00:34:05.776 --> 00:34:09.936
- So why all this traffic? - To amuse
myself. I need some action every night.

410
00:34:11.574 --> 00:34:14.232
- Where does this door go?
- To the butcher shop.

411
00:34:14.319 --> 00:34:17.029
- The butcher's there? - No, never on
Wednesdays. That's Follies night.

412
00:34:17.134 --> 00:34:21.225
- What Follies? - It's a cinema. He goes
every Wednesday with his wife.

413
00:34:21.405 --> 00:34:23.207
I told you they're not in!

414
00:34:30.086 --> 00:34:32.202
Go on, go home. Go on.

415
00:35:47.636 --> 00:35:49.016
What are you doing here?

416
00:35:49.734 --> 00:35:50.783
And you?

417
00:35:51.045 --> 00:35:54.612
- I thought you were at Follies.
- Too tired, thanks to you.

418
00:35:54.857 --> 00:35:56.447
I changed my mind.

419
00:35:58.485 --> 00:35:59.604
What time is it?

420
00:35:59.726 --> 00:36:03.380
Time to get up. We're going for
a little walk. Get dressed.

421
00:36:05.680 --> 00:36:08.232
Get undressed, get dressed...

422
00:36:10.110 --> 00:36:11.684
Where are we going?

423
00:36:11.894 --> 00:36:14.202
- Police headquarters.
- Again?

424
00:36:15.041 --> 00:36:17.105
This is becoming an obsession.

425
00:36:17.236 --> 00:36:19.701
How regularly will you be picking me up?

426
00:36:19.824 --> 00:36:23.565
- Note that this is the second time.
- That's precisely why.

427
00:36:26.738 --> 00:36:28.854
Do you often take sleeping pills?

428
00:36:29.851 --> 00:36:32.473
When I want to sleep and I'm anxious.

429
00:36:33.146 --> 00:36:36.013
As it happens, since the other night,
I <i>am</i> anxious.

430
00:36:36.284 --> 00:36:37.822
Whose fault is that?

431
00:36:43.836 --> 00:36:44.901
Hurry up.

432
00:36:45.321 --> 00:36:47.008
Hurry up, hurry up...

433
00:36:49.088 --> 00:36:52.476
- Damnit! I'm too thick. I'm not going!
- You got the wrong foot.

434
00:36:54.424 --> 00:36:57.554
I'm not going!
I'm going back to sleep.

435
00:37:00.850 --> 00:37:02.423
Want to be carried?

436
00:37:14.887 --> 00:37:16.636
Gentlemen, to the left.

437
00:37:19.556 --> 00:37:21.024
Hello, Marcel.

438
00:37:22.556 --> 00:37:24.113
Café Saint-Michel.

439
00:37:26.386 --> 00:37:27.959
Are you working?

440
00:37:30.075 --> 00:37:32.103
Be reasonable.
Go to sleep.

441
00:37:34.551 --> 00:37:36.562
No, as a matter of fact.

442
00:37:37.121 --> 00:37:39.044
That's why I'm calling.

443
00:37:39.595 --> 00:37:42.480
I ran into the Martin-Prévels.

444
00:37:42.620 --> 00:37:44.193
Yes, the whole gang.

445
00:37:44.770 --> 00:37:47.436
We'll end up in a nightclub,
you know them.

446
00:37:49.516 --> 00:37:51.108
Three, four hours.

447
00:37:52.241 --> 00:37:54.042
Thérese sends her love.

448
00:37:54.355 --> 00:37:56.630
No, no, don't wait up.
I have my key.

449
00:37:56.787 --> 00:37:59.391
Yes, that's right.
Good night, dear.

450
00:39:33.088 --> 00:39:35.571
You won't follow me to my bedroom, no?

451
00:39:35.737 --> 00:39:37.835
Enough. What do you want?

452
00:39:38.832 --> 00:39:41.839
If my husband is paying you,
I can pay as well.

453
00:39:44.059 --> 00:39:47.171
You know where I was.
You could forget about it.

454
00:39:48.063 --> 00:39:49.934
Things like that happen.

455
00:39:50.720 --> 00:39:52.416
How much do you want?

456
00:39:53.842 --> 00:39:55.940
Oh, do whatever you want!

457
00:40:01.753 --> 00:40:05.897
If some thread had stayed behind,
we might have gotten something out of it...

458
00:40:07.275 --> 00:40:10.405
The shape is distinctive,
the edge is thick.

459
00:40:10.632 --> 00:40:12.782
It's not a common make.

460
00:40:14.408 --> 00:40:18.535
You should see the Paris Button Shop.
They'll tell you more than I can.

461
00:40:19.147 --> 00:40:23.361
If it's theirs, they'll know right away
which tailors purchased it.

462
00:40:23.694 --> 00:40:27.086
- And from the tailors...
- Yes, we'll see about that later.

463
00:40:28.170 --> 00:40:30.495
- You can say that again.
- Sorry.

464
00:40:41.360 --> 00:40:45.504
You can go home, but...
I won't be back in before 10 o'clock.

465
00:40:48.057 --> 00:40:49.211
Merde!

466
00:40:49.403 --> 00:40:50.994
I'd forgotten all about him.

467
00:40:52.454 --> 00:40:54.552
Try to shake him awake.

468
00:40:58.154 --> 00:40:59.220
What?

469
00:41:04.799 --> 00:41:06.862
How many pills did you take?

470
00:41:13.324 --> 00:41:15.090
What time did you go to sleep?

471
00:41:17.520 --> 00:41:18.569
Oh, it's you.

472
00:41:18.953 --> 00:41:20.667
He was about to go home.

473
00:41:20.807 --> 00:41:22.206
I'll put him on.

474
00:41:23.198 --> 00:41:24.230
Lagrume.

475
00:41:31.713 --> 00:41:33.112
Speaking!

476
00:41:33.225 --> 00:41:36.669
I wonder if it's worth the bother, sir.
A woman...

477
00:41:37.876 --> 00:41:39.607
She looked odd to me.

478
00:41:40.053 --> 00:41:44.213
In the end, a bourgeoise who spends the
night out, and cheats on her husband.

479
00:41:44.388 --> 00:41:47.832
Nightclub, champagne, gigolo,
then a love hotel.

480
00:41:48.129 --> 00:41:50.508
And then goes home, sight unseen.

481
00:41:50.703 --> 00:41:54.567
Except that she took me for a private
dick and offered me money.

482
00:41:54.969 --> 00:41:57.015
Anyway, I'll give you the address.

483
00:41:57.102 --> 00:41:58.134
Go ahead.

484
00:42:01.001 --> 00:42:02.348
Mme Morin?

485
00:42:03.152 --> 00:42:04.358
With an O?

486
00:42:05.302 --> 00:42:06.369
What?

487
00:42:07.173 --> 00:42:08.764
Maurin, A, U.

488
00:42:09.088 --> 00:42:11.326
That widow Maurin is an old cow!

489
00:42:11.483 --> 00:42:12.812
What did you say?

490
00:42:12.900 --> 00:42:14.490
One moment. Hold on.

491
00:42:15.312 --> 00:42:18.145
I said, the widow Maurin is an old cow!

492
00:42:18.494 --> 00:42:20.749
I was sure it was all her fault.

493
00:42:20.916 --> 00:42:24.291
- Who are you talking about?
- My bitch of a landlady.

494
00:42:25.323 --> 00:42:26.617
Rue Turenne.

495
00:42:32.774 --> 00:42:34.627
<i>The Widow Maurin.
(Owner)</i>

496
00:42:34.714 --> 00:42:35.885
Lagrume?

497
00:42:36.385 --> 00:42:37.767
Where are you?

498
00:42:39.446 --> 00:42:41.596
Wait for me. I'm coming over.

499
00:42:42.391 --> 00:42:43.458
No reason.

500
00:42:45.399 --> 00:42:47.374
Okay, take him home...

501
00:42:47.654 --> 00:42:49.892
Without waking him up, if possible.

502
00:43:07.623 --> 00:43:11.208
To live here, and have it off with a
gigolo in a furnished room on Rue Etoile?

503
00:43:11.317 --> 00:43:12.772
Takes a special kind.

504
00:43:12.874 --> 00:43:15.585
- Does the name Maurin ring a bell?
- Huh?

505
00:43:15.689 --> 00:43:18.470
What's the name of your
butcher's landlady?

506
00:43:18.610 --> 00:43:20.043
You think that...?

507
00:43:20.847 --> 00:43:24.108
- Come on, let's go.
- But it's barely 6 o'clock, sir.

508
00:43:25.035 --> 00:43:26.713
The best time to go fishing.

509
00:43:26.835 --> 00:43:29.249
But we have no warrant.
You know the law.

510
00:43:29.336 --> 00:43:31.949
<i>I</i> do, but we aren't going up to my place.

511
00:43:38.641 --> 00:43:39.760
10th floor.

512
00:43:44.262 --> 00:43:45.504
Mme Maurin?

513
00:43:46.780 --> 00:43:47.811
Police.

514
00:43:56.326 --> 00:43:57.011
No!

515
00:43:57.261 --> 00:44:00.164
This time, you've gone too far.
The joke is not funny anymore.

516
00:44:00.276 --> 00:44:04.140
Rest assured, this isn't a joke. I'd just
like to chat with you for 5 minutes.

517
00:44:05.413 --> 00:44:09.435
This makes no sense! This is despicable.
I don't see how my private life...

518
00:44:09.705 --> 00:44:13.823
You may have misunderstood me, Maam. I'm
not here about Rue Etoile, but Rue Rosiers.

519
00:44:14.286 --> 00:44:16.331
Rue Etoile doesn't bother me at all.

520
00:44:16.442 --> 00:44:20.479
What bothers me is... First of all, it's
to be telling you all this on the landing.

521
00:44:36.460 --> 00:44:38.278
My husband is sleeping.

522
00:44:38.558 --> 00:44:42.710
We won't wake him up. Not right away.
We may need to speak to him as well...

523
00:44:43.602 --> 00:44:47.789
Oh, not about our little adventures.
Those are private. Our secret.

524
00:44:48.360 --> 00:44:51.835
A young woman can have an affair.
It doesn't concern the Crime Squad.

525
00:44:51.940 --> 00:44:54.003
- Crime Squad?
- Oh, yes.

526
00:44:54.108 --> 00:44:55.524
It's reassuring and it's not.

527
00:44:55.593 --> 00:44:59.764
Because it rules out the Rue Etoile side
of things, but not the Rue Rosiers side.

528
00:45:00.305 --> 00:45:02.700
Last night, you were on Rue Rosiers.

529
00:45:02.806 --> 00:45:06.233
Nothing extraordinary in that.
In fact, I was there too.

530
00:45:06.625 --> 00:45:09.964
But it's precisely this coincidence
that's troubling me.

531
00:45:10.156 --> 00:45:12.832
So, maybe you'll be able
to explain it to me.

532
00:45:12.937 --> 00:45:15.856
I don't understand.
It's so simple.

533
00:45:16.744 --> 00:45:18.387
I wasn't expecting this.

534
00:45:19.917 --> 00:45:21.753
I have no idea where we are.

535
00:45:21.884 --> 00:45:24.908
Well, we haven't moved.
Still on Rue Rosiers.

536
00:45:26.114 --> 00:45:29.070
Last night, I ate at my parents'
in the 4th district.

537
00:45:29.175 --> 00:45:32.287
- Rue Turenne?
- No. Rue Turenne is my mother-in-law's.

538
00:45:33.863 --> 00:45:37.307
My parents live on Blvd Beaumarchais.
I was born in that neighborhood.

539
00:45:37.570 --> 00:45:39.615
That's where I met my husband.

540
00:45:39.754 --> 00:45:43.269
Coming home, I went by Rue Rosiers,
which was on the way.

541
00:45:44.170 --> 00:45:47.789
I saw a crowd there,
and I stopped to look.

542
00:45:47.999 --> 00:45:49.538
Like any Parisian would.

543
00:45:50.544 --> 00:45:53.691
I must have stayed around...
10 minutes or so.

544
00:45:55.125 --> 00:45:56.174
Then...

545
00:45:56.873 --> 00:45:58.919
Then I had that rendezvous.

546
00:45:59.067 --> 00:46:00.378
Your husband...

547
00:46:00.816 --> 00:46:03.858
Your husband didn't find it unusual
for you to come home at 5 a.m.?

548
00:46:05.116 --> 00:46:08.386
I called him around midnight,
and told him a story.

549
00:46:09.531 --> 00:46:11.647
He was still working.

550
00:46:11.751 --> 00:46:13.290
When I came in,
he was asleep,

551
00:46:13.325 --> 00:46:14.968
so I didn't wake him up.

552
00:46:16.411 --> 00:46:20.817
You're putting me in an awkward situation.
I was just about to ask you to do it.

553
00:46:20.922 --> 00:46:23.982
- I...
- No! Nothing about our little secret.

554
00:46:24.279 --> 00:46:26.918
Just some information.
A couple of questions.

555
00:46:39.494 --> 00:46:42.099
- Is it really necessary?
- Really.

556
00:46:42.693 --> 00:46:44.284
In that case...

557
00:46:47.580 --> 00:46:50.202
Forgive me. I was in such a state
I forgot to ask...

558
00:46:50.273 --> 00:46:51.671
Inspector Maigret.

559
00:46:52.396 --> 00:46:54.057
And Detective Lagrume.

560
00:47:05.574 --> 00:47:08.721
What do you think, sir?
Rather comfortable, eh?

561
00:47:13.013 --> 00:47:14.621
Money is a nice thing.

562
00:47:14.832 --> 00:47:17.944
They say it doesn't bring happiness.
But still...

563
00:47:19.028 --> 00:47:20.898
I said, "Still..."

564
00:47:23.775 --> 00:47:24.597
Look.

565
00:47:24.965 --> 00:47:26.574
A little Normand.

566
00:47:28.899 --> 00:47:30.629
I like Normand landscapes.

567
00:47:30.647 --> 00:47:33.707
My husband will see you.
He's getting dressed.

568
00:47:35.929 --> 00:47:37.764
Are you fans of the Basque style?

569
00:47:37.904 --> 00:47:40.073
Yes, we were just talking about it.

570
00:47:40.597 --> 00:47:42.835
My husband painted that last night.

571
00:47:42.992 --> 00:47:45.125
When I left, he was still sketching it.

572
00:47:45.231 --> 00:47:46.769
What time did you go out?

573
00:47:46.836 --> 00:47:47.815
Around 7.

574
00:47:47.920 --> 00:47:52.090
Say, Lagrume, do you realize?
Between 7 and midnight. He works quickly.

575
00:47:52.335 --> 00:47:54.170
Quickly and much too much.

576
00:47:54.609 --> 00:47:56.410
Much too much for his health.

577
00:47:56.567 --> 00:47:59.373
Forgive me. I took that over there.
If you have a piece of paper...

578
00:47:59.417 --> 00:48:02.371
- No matter. You can just put it back.
- Thank you.

579
00:48:02.520 --> 00:48:06.227
So what exactly does
an architect-decorator do?

580
00:48:09.905 --> 00:48:12.597
Sorry to have kept you waiting,
gentlemen.

581
00:48:13.874 --> 00:48:15.272
Marcel Maurin.

582
00:48:15.517 --> 00:48:19.198
- I'm embarrassed to greet you in this...
- And I, to get you out of bed at this hour,

583
00:48:19.303 --> 00:48:22.555
especially since my visit is not strictly
official.

584
00:48:22.660 --> 00:48:26.384
- Did your wife inform you?
- Yes, she spoke of murders.

585
00:48:27.345 --> 00:48:30.379
We're going to have another
one of those days...

586
00:48:33.046 --> 00:48:35.196
- I beg your pardon.
- It's nothing.

587
00:48:35.284 --> 00:48:36.857
What is this about?

588
00:48:42.977 --> 00:48:44.289
Before anything else...

589
00:48:44.393 --> 00:48:48.685
it's my duty to warn you that your
answers may have serious consequences.

590
00:48:49.052 --> 00:48:50.644
Serious?

591
00:48:51.211 --> 00:48:53.029
Not for you, of course.

592
00:48:53.685 --> 00:48:55.118
For Barberot.

593
00:48:55.827 --> 00:48:57.523
- May I?
- Please.

594
00:48:59.655 --> 00:49:02.278
Barberot.
The butcher on Rue Turenne.

595
00:49:02.786 --> 00:49:04.577
Do you know him well?

596
00:49:04.683 --> 00:49:07.655
"Well," you know...
I know him like I know many people.

597
00:49:07.856 --> 00:49:10.968
M. Maurin, I won't try to pull
the wool over your eyes.

598
00:49:11.099 --> 00:49:13.722
You've heard of the crimes
in the Marais?

599
00:49:14.141 --> 00:49:15.960
The papers say someone was arrested.

600
00:49:16.135 --> 00:49:19.806
- It wasn't the right person.
- So... Barberot...

601
00:49:20.308 --> 00:49:23.468
He's not been charged.
He's just a suspect. A strong one.

602
00:49:23.752 --> 00:49:25.325
Barberot, a suspect?

603
00:49:26.331 --> 00:49:27.563
You're surprised?

604
00:49:27.860 --> 00:49:29.084
I'm amused.

605
00:49:31.758 --> 00:49:34.557
Barberot, that idiot!
No, that's too funny.

606
00:49:34.766 --> 00:49:36.899
Don't you think it's fantastic?

607
00:49:37.004 --> 00:49:37.843
Here!

608
00:49:42.372 --> 00:49:43.945
Here's Barberot!

609
00:49:45.956 --> 00:49:47.092
In all his splendor!

610
00:49:47.110 --> 00:49:48.623
In all his glory!

611
00:49:49.339 --> 00:49:51.070
There! The calf's head.

612
00:49:51.708 --> 00:49:54.523
Yes, that's him.
I was an assistant back then.

613
00:49:54.628 --> 00:49:58.370
Oh, he could have put on Chinese eyes or
a cuckold's horns. He took what was handy.

614
00:49:59.410 --> 00:50:01.474
You must admit it's surprising.

615
00:50:01.948 --> 00:50:04.134
Not really, when you know him.

616
00:50:04.343 --> 00:50:07.683
- But that's my butcher shop!
- Yours? Oh, really!?

617
00:50:08.155 --> 00:50:11.092
Yes, the old Maurin shop
became Barberot's.

618
00:50:11.191 --> 00:50:14.609
- When my father-in-law died...
- "My husband didn't succeed him, etc."

619
00:50:15.320 --> 00:50:18.013
- So, in the middle, that's your father.
- Yes, it is.

620
00:50:18.275 --> 00:50:20.128
- And that's you.
- Yes.

621
00:50:20.225 --> 00:50:23.512
Wow, you're really looking at your dad.
It's nice to see this kind of admiration.

622
00:50:24.779 --> 00:50:27.315
- And there's mom.
- Ah, no!

623
00:50:28.329 --> 00:50:29.368
That, no.

624
00:50:29.840 --> 00:50:32.935
That's not my mother's style.
Not at all.

625
00:50:34.766 --> 00:50:37.861
No. That, that's Mauricette.
The check-out girl.

626
00:50:39.652 --> 00:50:40.876
Pretty woman.

627
00:50:41.033 --> 00:50:44.626
Well then, M. Maurin, it's time for us
to thank you for agreeing to see us.

628
00:50:44.748 --> 00:50:46.549
I came hoping for a prosecution witness.

629
00:50:46.654 --> 00:50:49.224
But I must admit that calf's head
was quite disarming.

630
00:50:49.356 --> 00:50:53.027
It doesn't correspond at all to the
image I have of my killer.

631
00:50:56.105 --> 00:50:58.151
- I apologize.
- Not at all.

632
00:50:58.368 --> 00:51:00.781
If I can be of help in any way...

633
00:51:01.358 --> 00:51:02.634
Well...

634
00:51:03.194 --> 00:51:06.270
I feel I'm about to take advantage of
your kindness again.

635
00:51:06.367 --> 00:51:09.890
It may seem silly to you.
But I'd like to see your suits.

636
00:51:12.311 --> 00:51:15.056
Well, the surprises just keep coming.

637
00:51:15.162 --> 00:51:18.064
Nothing could be easier.
This way, please.

638
00:51:27.166 --> 00:51:29.841
Wow.
This is what I call a wardrobe.

639
00:51:29.982 --> 00:51:32.481
- Take a look, Lagrume.
- In spite of what they say...

640
00:51:32.551 --> 00:51:34.422
- Tux?
- That's not necessary.

641
00:51:42.461 --> 00:51:44.507
All very high quality.

642
00:51:45.591 --> 00:51:47.322
Oh, of course!
Bernheim & Son.

643
00:51:47.909 --> 00:51:50.260
An expensive tailor saves
in the long run.

644
00:51:50.810 --> 00:51:54.027
Price gets forgotten,
but quality remains. So they say.

645
00:51:57.963 --> 00:52:00.935
Not to be indiscreet, but which one
did you wear last night?

646
00:52:01.005 --> 00:52:03.296
I didn't wear one.
I didn't go out.

647
00:52:03.400 --> 00:52:06.810
Generally, when I'm working, I just
wear a smock and some old slacks.

648
00:52:06.993 --> 00:52:07.815
Okay.

649
00:52:08.270 --> 00:52:10.753
In any case, you only have
those six suits?

650
00:52:10.875 --> 00:52:11.889
Yes, alas.

651
00:52:12.195 --> 00:52:13.821
Okey-dokey.

652
00:52:14.205 --> 00:52:15.640
So here we are.

653
00:52:19.408 --> 00:52:22.118
I don't know what
you're searching for, Inspector, but...

654
00:52:22.975 --> 00:52:24.574
You're searching well.

655
00:52:25.868 --> 00:52:28.386
- Don't you want anything else?
- No.

656
00:52:31.644 --> 00:52:33.269
I've really abused your kindness.

657
00:52:33.374 --> 00:52:36.399
Please be good enough to offer
my excuses to Mme Maurin.

658
00:52:36.504 --> 00:52:38.497
You can count on me.

659
00:52:39.013 --> 00:52:40.622
Goodbye, gentlemen.

660
00:53:01.676 --> 00:53:03.075
Have they gone?

661
00:53:05.322 --> 00:53:07.595
Why did they want to see your suits?

662
00:53:07.717 --> 00:53:11.197
- Where were you last night?
- I told you on the phone.

663
00:53:11.897 --> 00:53:15.021
Oh yes, I forgot.
With the Martin-Prévels.

664
00:53:15.984 --> 00:53:17.801
- Thérese is well.
- Yes.

665
00:53:17.915 --> 00:53:22.084
I'm not asking. I'm telling you. After
you rang, I called the Martin-Prévels.

666
00:53:22.618 --> 00:53:24.680
They were already in bed.

667
00:53:25.188 --> 00:53:26.744
You too, I suppose.

668
00:53:26.989 --> 00:53:28.597
Where? With whom?

669
00:53:30.013 --> 00:53:32.854
I was followed all night.
By that little detective.

670
00:53:33.467 --> 00:53:34.603
So what?

671
00:53:35.730 --> 00:53:36.779
So I...

672
00:53:37.339 --> 00:53:40.468
I thought it best not to lead him
all the way here.

673
00:53:41.623 --> 00:53:42.916
I tried to waste time.

674
00:53:43.520 --> 00:53:46.860
I know your method of wasting time!
With whom this time?

675
00:53:46.947 --> 00:53:51.178
With what kind of thug? Picked up where?
Admit it, you little skank!

676
00:53:52.198 --> 00:53:55.468
So you're back at it again.
You had to start again!

677
00:53:56.149 --> 00:53:59.139
You like them, those brutes,
those roughnecks.

678
00:53:59.243 --> 00:54:00.800
You like those apes!

679
00:54:01.245 --> 00:54:04.287
So say it, you little slut!
Say it!

680
00:54:07.059 --> 00:54:08.615
Do you want me to slap you?

681
00:54:08.702 --> 00:54:10.600
Tell me, do you want a slap?

682
00:54:11.701 --> 00:54:13.432
Do you admit you deserve it?

683
00:54:14.594 --> 00:54:15.643
Yes.

684
00:54:19.088 --> 00:54:20.119
I said, yes!

685
00:54:23.607 --> 00:54:25.565
Slut! Slut! Slut!

686
00:54:28.441 --> 00:54:30.539
Come on, come on.
It's over.

687
00:54:31.755 --> 00:54:33.119
Calm down.

688
00:54:36.616 --> 00:54:37.804
Don't cry.

689
00:54:37.892 --> 00:54:40.567
I want to know.
I want you to tell me.

690
00:54:40.952 --> 00:54:42.210
Of course.

691
00:54:42.877 --> 00:54:44.205
Do you promise?

692
00:54:44.310 --> 00:54:46.426
- What?
- You'll tell me.

693
00:54:46.671 --> 00:54:47.912
I promise.

694
00:54:49.398 --> 00:54:50.937
My little Marcel.

695
00:54:51.915 --> 00:54:54.240
Why put yourself in such a state?

696
00:54:55.028 --> 00:54:56.706
Are you so unhappy?

697
00:54:57.336 --> 00:54:59.434
There, there.
It's over.

698
00:55:02.432 --> 00:55:04.251
I want you to tell me!

699
00:55:07.346 --> 00:55:08.901
You promised!

700
00:55:59.553 --> 00:56:02.412
Catch the palefaces
and cut off their heads!

701
00:57:36.793 --> 00:57:38.059
What is it?

702
00:57:41.075 --> 00:57:43.804
Wow, you really have a
knack for being there.

703
00:57:43.890 --> 00:57:46.706
Come open up for me.
You have the key for that door?

704
00:57:46.846 --> 00:57:49.766
No. But Mme Vignole is bound to have it.

705
00:57:50.238 --> 00:57:51.950
Don't move.
I'll be down.

706
00:57:52.064 --> 00:57:56.211
This is a new trend. There's a perfectly
fine entrance for everyone else.

707
00:57:57.138 --> 00:57:59.953
After that fuss last night, you'd think
we'd finally have some peace.

708
00:58:00.059 --> 00:58:01.824
Are you the only one with this key?

709
00:58:01.930 --> 00:58:04.528
Sure. I've never used it.
This door was sealed off.

710
00:58:04.685 --> 00:58:07.036
<i>M. Barberot,
someone needs a leg of lamb!</i>

711
00:58:07.211 --> 00:58:09.362
- Er... may I?
- Yes. Go ahead.

712
00:58:10.114 --> 00:58:12.194
May I?
I'll return it later.

713
00:58:16.102 --> 00:58:19.136
Have you seen <i>Le Parisien</i>?
It talks about your methods.

714
00:58:19.249 --> 00:58:21.224
Is Mme Maurin home?

715
00:58:22.037 --> 00:58:26.163
Ah, she must be eating right now. And so
should I. I have noodles cooking.

716
00:58:26.723 --> 00:58:29.852
According to <i>Le Parisien,
your suspect is a ploy.</i>

717
00:58:32.169 --> 00:58:34.005
I didn't tell you where.

718
00:58:34.442 --> 00:58:36.557
4th floor, on the right.

719
00:58:39.451 --> 00:58:40.483
Mme Maurin?

720
00:58:41.251 --> 00:58:44.854
Inspector Maigret, Crime Squad.
I have a few questions to ask you.

721
00:58:47.056 --> 00:58:48.368
About what?

722
00:58:49.005 --> 00:58:51.891
Er, something that concerns you.
Well...

723
00:58:52.712 --> 00:58:56.366
I should say, something that concerns
the building's owner.

724
00:58:59.051 --> 00:59:00.694
Something to do with keys.

725
00:59:00.799 --> 00:59:03.894
As building owner, you have the keys
to the building?

726
00:59:04.191 --> 00:59:05.310
Naturally.

727
00:59:06.839 --> 00:59:09.078
- Here they are.
- Thank you.

728
00:59:09.200 --> 00:59:12.399
I also have the keys to the cellar
and to the guardhouse.

729
00:59:16.937 --> 00:59:18.703
What about the small door?

730
00:59:19.875 --> 00:59:22.218
Er, behind the trash bin downstairs.

731
00:59:22.707 --> 00:59:25.705
Ah, no.
I suppose the concierge must have it.

732
00:59:25.792 --> 00:59:26.999
- Not you?
- No.

733
00:59:27.156 --> 00:59:29.734
- That's odd. I was told you had it.
- Really?

734
00:59:29.840 --> 00:59:32.655
- May I ask by whom?
- The butcher downstairs.

735
00:59:33.144 --> 00:59:34.193
Barberot?

736
00:59:35.408 --> 00:59:37.821
What business is it
of this buffoon's?

737
00:59:38.503 --> 00:59:41.440
Oh, he's probably mistaken.
He was just talking.

738
00:59:41.772 --> 00:59:45.164
Say, since we're talking about him,
I'd like to ask you for some information.

739
00:59:45.383 --> 00:59:47.079
About his character.

740
00:59:48.460 --> 00:59:49.561
His character?

741
00:59:49.719 --> 00:59:52.122
You can always amend your statement
later on.

742
00:59:52.244 --> 00:59:54.754
I wouldn't want my words
to be misconstrued.

743
00:59:54.877 --> 00:59:57.516
Barberot is neither good nor bad.
He's a butcher.

744
00:59:57.919 --> 01:00:00.943
Unfortunately, people always come
to resemble those they live with.

745
01:00:01.047 --> 01:00:03.398
- And when you live with a trollop...
- Oh yeah?

746
01:00:03.556 --> 01:00:05.793
- Do you know the checkout girl?
- No.

747
01:00:05.899 --> 01:00:09.116
You're not missing anything.
Well. It remains to be seen.

748
01:00:09.946 --> 01:00:13.049
She'll sleep with anything and anyone.

749
01:00:13.800 --> 01:00:17.437
- Barberot included.
- It's normal with him. She married him.

750
01:00:17.956 --> 01:00:22.381
That kind of woman always finds a taker.
Everyone visits. An idiot eventually buys.

751
01:00:22.590 --> 01:00:26.034
But... She already worked there
back in your husband's time.

752
01:00:30.064 --> 01:00:33.228
- May I? I have some vegetables cooking.
- Please.

753
01:00:40.811 --> 01:00:42.035
I apologize for

754
01:00:42.036 --> 01:00:43.669
bothering you during your meal.

755
01:00:44.159 --> 01:00:45.750
Oh, it's no bother.

756
01:00:46.466 --> 01:00:48.443
The meals of a woman alone.

757
01:00:48.538 --> 01:00:50.620
I don't even set the table anymore.

758
01:00:57.197 --> 01:01:00.099
- It must have left a void.
- What's that?

759
01:01:00.361 --> 01:01:02.022
Your son's departure.

760
01:01:02.739 --> 01:01:05.921
- Eventually, children must get married.
- Do you know my son?

761
01:01:06.384 --> 01:01:09.479
I think so.
A charming young man.

762
01:01:11.568 --> 01:01:13.666
What does he have to do with you?

763
01:01:14.628 --> 01:01:17.460
This same investigation. I've been
asking questions here and there.

764
01:01:18.369 --> 01:01:19.716
Buy why him?

765
01:01:19.933 --> 01:01:23.595
Why him. Why you. That's all
part of the investigation.

766
01:01:23.867 --> 01:01:25.432
The amusing part.

767
01:01:25.887 --> 01:01:29.498
Marcel showed me a photo of the butcher
shop. The one with the calf's head.

768
01:01:29.691 --> 01:01:30.844
We had a laugh.

769
01:01:31.359 --> 01:01:33.772
Then we talked about you, about dad.

770
01:01:33.886 --> 01:01:35.582
A remarkable man.

771
01:01:35.757 --> 01:01:38.886
I mean, your son. Sensitive.
An artist.

772
01:01:40.250 --> 01:01:42.103
You don't really know him.

773
01:01:42.261 --> 01:01:43.414
No one does.

774
01:01:44.821 --> 01:01:46.543
He painted this at 14.

775
01:01:46.876 --> 01:01:49.848
Have you ever seen anything like this?
At 14!?

776
01:01:50.879 --> 01:01:53.835
Wow, I confess it's only
because you're telling me.

777
01:01:54.770 --> 01:01:58.040
- There was something I didn't understand
until now. - What's that?

778
01:01:58.337 --> 01:01:59.719
Why he didn't follow in

779
01:01:59.720 --> 01:02:00.750
dad's footsteps.

780
01:02:00.855 --> 01:02:02.726
You can't be serious.

781
01:02:03.268 --> 01:02:04.999
Marcel, a butcher?

782
01:02:05.112 --> 01:02:09.081
Imagine Marcel as a butcher cutting meat,
chatting up neighborhood gossips,

783
01:02:09.185 --> 01:02:13.355
maybe with Mauricette at the register.
That's impossible. You can't imagine it.

784
01:02:13.460 --> 01:02:15.471
How could you think for one minute...?

785
01:02:17.013 --> 01:02:18.516
Eh. I didn't think.

786
01:02:19.460 --> 01:02:21.156
If he had persisted...

787
01:02:21.961 --> 01:02:25.090
Or rather, if <i>they</i> had let him persist...

788
01:02:25.335 --> 01:02:28.656
my son would be today a great painter,
or a great sculptor.

789
01:02:28.761 --> 01:02:31.226
Because he had the choice, you see,
the choice!

790
01:02:31.331 --> 01:02:34.469
- When you're gifted...
- Come. You'll see. Come.

791
01:02:44.231 --> 01:02:46.312
Here. Take a look at this.

792
01:02:50.551 --> 01:02:52.334
Take a good look at this.

793
01:02:52.998 --> 01:02:54.013
At 13!

794
01:02:55.726 --> 01:02:57.317
At that, at 12.

795
01:02:58.655 --> 01:03:01.906
Here. Even before he could read,
he would play sonatas on this.

796
01:03:02.047 --> 01:03:06.172
- Wow. Even music, eh?
- I had him tutored in piano, violin...

797
01:03:07.651 --> 01:03:10.395
- Then he developed a passion for modeling.
- Oh.

798
01:03:10.875 --> 01:03:13.516
There too, if only he had carried on...

799
01:03:14.337 --> 01:03:17.143
But in the end,
he embraced interior decor?

800
01:03:17.265 --> 01:03:19.328
- Oh, it wasn't his choice.
- No?

801
01:03:19.433 --> 01:03:21.540
<i>They</i> found a way to convince him.

802
01:03:21.750 --> 01:03:22.991
He's just a child.

803
01:03:23.480 --> 01:03:27.375
- Even his toys are there.
- Yes, he's held on to his sensitivity.

804
01:03:27.846 --> 01:03:30.801
This, he made last Christmas.
For me.

805
01:03:32.147 --> 01:03:35.277
Whenever he's here,
it's as if he's recapturing...

806
01:03:36.587 --> 01:03:37.654
Excuse me.

807
01:03:37.811 --> 01:03:40.452
Please.
In any case, I'll be leaving.

808
01:03:51.525 --> 01:03:54.130
It's for you.
You have a call at the butcher's.

809
01:03:54.479 --> 01:03:56.595
Oh yes, I left the address.

810
01:03:57.242 --> 01:03:58.414
This is fun.

811
01:03:58.948 --> 01:04:02.636
- And you still put in water.
- He does. Last time he was here...

812
01:04:03.091 --> 01:04:04.052
Yesterday?

813
01:04:05.783 --> 01:04:08.773
Yesterday? No! Not yesterday.
I haven't seen my son in weeks.

814
01:04:08.930 --> 01:04:09.857
Are you sure?

815
01:04:10.521 --> 01:04:11.902
Of course I'm sure!

816
01:04:14.184 --> 01:04:16.754
Oh, I must have thought
your son said, yesterday.

817
01:04:16.946 --> 01:04:20.111
I talk, I talk. And my call is still
waiting. Excuse me.

818
01:04:25.265 --> 01:04:26.296
Thank you.

819
01:04:27.922 --> 01:04:29.024
Hello. Boss?

820
01:04:29.233 --> 01:04:31.943
You sure took your time.
Where were you?

821
01:04:32.178 --> 01:04:35.850
I want to talk about the other one, the
young one. I'm at the listening post.

822
01:04:35.972 --> 01:04:38.070
Are you interested in
Yvonne Maurin's calls?

823
01:04:38.071 --> 01:04:38.857
Yes.

824
01:04:39.373 --> 01:04:41.602
Let me get something to write with.

825
01:04:42.100 --> 01:04:44.190
You look even better as a blonde.

826
01:04:44.295 --> 01:04:47.791
- You've seen me as a brunette?
- In a photo.

827
01:04:48.342 --> 01:04:49.356
Go ahead.

828
01:04:54.277 --> 01:04:55.851
She called him twice?

829
01:04:55.852 --> 01:04:56.533
Yes.

830
01:04:57.092 --> 01:05:00.711
The first time, she got a cleaning woman
who didn't know anything.

831
01:05:01.053 --> 01:05:05.773
The second time, a young man replied that
M. Georges couldn't be awakened before 3.

832
01:05:09.908 --> 01:05:11.272
What is it?

833
01:05:13.913 --> 01:05:15.031
Well, what is it?

834
01:05:16.202 --> 01:05:18.336
- Maigret. Crime.
- Wow.

835
01:05:19.726 --> 01:05:23.135
- What does Crime want with me?
- Oh, you know. May I?

836
01:05:28.827 --> 01:05:29.753
So.

837
01:05:31.624 --> 01:05:33.722
Were you napping or sleeping in?

838
01:05:36.799 --> 01:05:40.943
- I didn't disturb you at work, I hope.
- Oh, just a friend, an acquaintance.

839
01:05:41.346 --> 01:05:43.776
At work? What does that mean?
I have a trade?

840
01:05:43.932 --> 01:05:45.873
Oh, I do believe you have a trade.

841
01:05:45.978 --> 01:05:49.055
- If you want to see my papers...
- Oh, I know your paper.

842
01:05:49.160 --> 01:05:53.374
Georges Vacher, alias Jo the Dancer,
alias Jojo Tango, 37, bachelor.

843
01:05:53.566 --> 01:05:55.174
Charm dancer. See?

844
01:05:55.541 --> 01:05:59.195
OK. Now you're going to tell me
very nicely what you did last night.

845
01:05:59.309 --> 01:06:00.358
In detail.

846
01:06:00.515 --> 01:06:02.579
I had dinner at 9 at La Cucaracha.

847
01:06:02.683 --> 01:06:04.047
- Alone?
- Yes.

848
01:06:04.240 --> 01:06:06.005
We can check.
And then?

849
01:06:06.775 --> 01:06:09.031
I left there around 1 in the morning.

850
01:06:09.144 --> 01:06:11.103
- Still alone?
- No.

851
01:06:11.627 --> 01:06:13.743
- A lady?
- I give you my word.

852
01:06:14.180 --> 01:06:15.753
Oh, I believe you.

853
01:06:16.785 --> 01:06:17.869
So, this lady...

854
01:06:18.377 --> 01:06:19.617
I'm listening.

855
01:06:20.059 --> 01:06:23.294
Oh, the classic story.
A bourgeoise on the town.

856
01:06:24.255 --> 01:06:25.846
They're all the same.

857
01:06:26.554 --> 01:06:30.698
A husband who neglects them. One night,
they have one drink too many, and...

858
01:06:30.926 --> 01:06:32.490
One hour of dreams.

859
01:06:32.958 --> 01:06:33.990
One hour of dreams.

860
01:06:34.531 --> 01:06:35.564
Anyway.

861
01:06:35.878 --> 01:06:38.491
- Did you have an appointment?
- No.

862
01:06:38.614 --> 01:06:39.942
But you knew her.

863
01:06:40.047 --> 01:06:43.072
Before last night, she had come
once before. Just once.

864
01:06:43.212 --> 01:06:46.717
- How long ago?
- If you think I take note of everything...

865
01:06:46.822 --> 01:06:50.127
Today, she tried to call you twice.
Why? Were you meeting again?

866
01:06:51.254 --> 01:06:52.828
No, I wouldn't think so.

867
01:06:53.063 --> 01:06:57.260
That poor woman has no luck. Her husband
neglects her and her lover disappoints.

868
01:06:58.544 --> 01:07:02.444
I could not disappoint her.
For the good reason that... nothing...

869
01:07:02.653 --> 01:07:04.244
What?
What are you mumbling?

870
01:07:04.471 --> 01:07:08.091
I never had a chance to disappoint her.
Because nothing happened.

871
01:07:09.078 --> 01:07:11.649
My word as a man.
Nothing at all.

872
01:07:12.513 --> 01:07:16.203
While dancing, she seemed to be
in a good mood and ready to go...

873
01:07:16.518 --> 01:07:18.415
She was even the one coming on.

874
01:07:18.608 --> 01:07:21.230
And then, once we got here, nothing.

875
01:07:22.305 --> 01:07:24.910
A piece of wood.
The line about a headache.

876
01:07:25.890 --> 01:07:28.163
I insisted, affectionately.

877
01:07:28.740 --> 01:07:30.873
I tried my best, but I think...
nothing...

878
01:07:31.440 --> 01:07:32.997
My God, articulate!

879
01:07:34.063 --> 01:07:37.683
- I said I tried my best...
- Why are you whispering like this?

880
01:07:38.907 --> 01:07:42.001
I'd rather not spread that around.
It's not good publicity.

881
01:07:42.753 --> 01:07:45.918
Women are so strange!
There are times when I...

882
01:07:46.337 --> 01:07:47.315
Yup.

883
01:07:47.455 --> 01:07:51.589
What can you do? You can't just live on
dreams. You have to learn to accept it.

884
01:07:51.957 --> 01:07:55.077
I hope for your sake
you didn't tell me tall tales.

885
01:07:57.796 --> 01:07:59.929
I don't even know that woman.

886
01:08:01.415 --> 01:08:02.988
What did she do?

887
01:08:12.928 --> 01:08:16.390
- Don't you have anything smaller?
- No, that's all I have.

888
01:08:18.943 --> 01:08:22.090
It doesn't matter. Take me back
to Quai Blériot. I forgot something.

889
01:08:34.652 --> 01:08:37.781
- The boss. I want to see him.
- Her. Who's asking?

890
01:08:37.973 --> 01:08:38.970
Police.

891
01:08:59.613 --> 01:09:02.428
Must be Mme Bailly
bringing back my iron.

892
01:09:08.120 --> 01:09:10.778
<i>Good evening,
ladies and gentlemen.</i>

893
01:09:10.935 --> 01:09:12.911
<i>Little news tonight.</i>

894
01:09:13.033 --> 01:09:16.678
<i>Political activity almost nil
on this blistering weekend.</i>

895
01:09:16.801 --> 01:09:18.759
<i>All of the country's energy</i>

896
01:09:18.890 --> 01:09:22.019
<i>seems focused on beaches
and river banks.</i>

897
01:09:24.310 --> 01:09:25.849
It's for you. Mme Maurin.

898
01:09:26.373 --> 01:09:28.961
- The old one?
- No. She's young.

899
01:09:33.952 --> 01:09:37.046
- She's in the living room?
- You know I have the dust covers on.

900
01:09:37.203 --> 01:09:41.365
- Ah, the dust covers.
- That's right. Rooms need vacations too.

901
01:09:42.953 --> 01:09:45.593
- You'll meet her like this?
- How else?

902
01:09:50.673 --> 01:09:54.345
- If you're eating, I can come back.
- Not at all. We've finished.

903
01:09:55.044 --> 01:09:55.971
I'm sorry to

904
01:09:55.972 --> 01:09:59.144
- disturb you.
- No, I'm sorry. I wasn't expecting you.

905
01:10:00.438 --> 01:10:01.513
Please.

906
01:10:06.408 --> 01:10:10.045
I realize how my visit must seem
unexpected, forward even.

907
01:10:10.832 --> 01:10:12.930
I'm sure it has a good reason.

908
01:10:15.360 --> 01:10:16.934
Even just this one.

909
01:10:18.945 --> 01:10:19.994
Wow.

910
01:10:21.664 --> 01:10:24.041
- Where did you find it?
- At home.

911
01:10:26.149 --> 01:10:27.302
Inspector...

912
01:10:28.028 --> 01:10:31.175
I don't know why you came
to Quai Blériot this morning.

913
01:10:31.883 --> 01:10:36.061
There are a lot of things that I don't
know, and that it's not my place to know.

914
01:10:37.216 --> 01:10:38.772
I do know what you think of me.

915
01:10:40.494 --> 01:10:44.673
I also know it's trite, very trite to say
I'm not the person you think I am.

916
01:10:47.006 --> 01:10:50.118
That's why I'd like to clear up
a misunderstanding, and...

917
01:10:50.346 --> 01:10:52.269
explain myself candidly

918
01:10:52.548 --> 01:10:53.554
freely.

919
01:10:54.096 --> 01:10:55.057
May I?

920
01:10:58.195 --> 01:11:00.276
Please! You can stay.

921
01:11:00.906 --> 01:11:02.234
You're welcome to.

922
01:11:02.496 --> 01:11:04.367
Why don't you bring in something?

923
01:11:04.455 --> 01:11:07.147
Some sloe gin,
straight from my wife's hometown.

924
01:11:07.803 --> 01:11:09.831
I'd like a drop, too.

925
01:11:11.343 --> 01:11:13.756
So, Mme Maurin, this misunderstanding...

926
01:11:16.204 --> 01:11:18.826
There's of course some truth in it.

927
01:11:20.513 --> 01:11:22.279
It's not easy to say.

928
01:11:22.567 --> 01:11:24.840
Better to get it over with, then.

929
01:11:26.064 --> 01:11:27.393
Yes, of course.

930
01:11:30.129 --> 01:11:32.734
I can imagine
what your detective told you.

931
01:11:35.252 --> 01:11:38.381
I can see him telling you
about the unfaithful wife,

932
01:11:39.439 --> 01:11:41.694
the bourgeoise who goes slumming,

933
01:11:43.145 --> 01:11:44.667
who has it off, as they say.

934
01:11:46.555 --> 01:11:48.548
To put it in the simplest terms.

935
01:11:48.645 --> 01:11:50.236
And it's not simple.

936
01:11:51.669 --> 01:11:54.800
It could be if I were, let's say,
an easy woman.

937
01:11:57.945 --> 01:12:00.952
You don't need to be very difficult
to have it off with...

938
01:12:01.652 --> 01:12:02.351
Eh?

939
01:12:03.339 --> 01:12:05.716
Maybe you need to be unhappy enough.

940
01:12:08.603 --> 01:12:11.016
He's been cheating on me for years.

941
01:12:12.571 --> 01:12:14.870
I put up with it for as long as I could.

942
01:12:16.453 --> 01:12:19.023
I know very well my husband's
good and bad qualities.

943
01:12:19.128 --> 01:12:20.980
At 12, I was already in love with him.

944
01:12:22.214 --> 01:12:23.158
He always was...

945
01:12:23.403 --> 01:12:26.008
much brighter,
much more brilliant than I.

946
01:12:27.585 --> 01:12:28.809
Women notice.

947
01:12:31.432 --> 01:12:33.530
To them, he's the artist.

948
01:12:35.391 --> 01:12:37.945
And I'm the little bourgeoise
hanging on.

949
01:12:38.847 --> 01:12:41.049
But you get tired of hanging on.

950
01:12:42.448 --> 01:12:45.035
It eventually becomes...
exhausting...

951
01:12:45.962 --> 01:12:47.281
humiliating, especially.

952
01:12:48.435 --> 01:12:49.205
And one day,

953
01:12:49.206 --> 01:12:51.819
an affair lasted longer
than the others.

954
01:12:53.927 --> 01:12:56.479
I learned that my friends knew about it.

955
01:12:58.245 --> 01:13:01.707
I was filled with an idiotic fury,
and I wanted to take revenge

956
01:13:02.353 --> 01:13:04.032
pay him back in kind.

957
01:13:06.585 --> 01:13:08.159
You probably don't understand.

958
01:13:09.068 --> 01:13:11.655
- But I do.
- I understand very well.

959
01:13:13.692 --> 01:13:15.790
I wanted to betray him

960
01:13:16.420 --> 01:13:18.745
with anyone, it didn't matter.

961
01:13:20.091 --> 01:13:21.840
But I betrayed myself,

962
01:13:23.290 --> 01:13:24.531
dismally.

963
01:13:26.612 --> 01:13:28.587
When you're not talented...

964
01:13:29.706 --> 01:13:32.854
I had gone out with friends.
I had drunk on purpose.

965
01:13:33.491 --> 01:13:34.942
I followed this...

966
01:13:35.205 --> 01:13:36.411
this Georges.

967
01:13:37.842 --> 01:13:38.873
One hour.

968
01:13:39.030 --> 01:13:39.940
Yesterday?

969
01:13:40.105 --> 01:13:40.840
No.

970
01:13:41.469 --> 01:13:43.601
It's been a few months.

971
01:13:44.013 --> 01:13:45.866
Nothing happened yesterday.

972
01:13:46.024 --> 01:13:48.970
- But you went back to Rue Etoile.
- That's true.

973
01:13:49.075 --> 01:13:51.400
- A kind of pilgrimage.
- Jules!

974
01:13:51.776 --> 01:13:54.382
No, he's right, Madame.
I deserved that.

975
01:13:56.584 --> 01:13:59.190
Yes, yesterday
I went back to Rue Etoile.

976
01:14:00.370 --> 01:14:02.923
But this time,
I left as I had arrived.

977
01:14:05.563 --> 01:14:07.644
When I saw that room again...

978
01:14:09.593 --> 01:14:13.230
I even asked myself how
there could have been a first time.

979
01:14:16.219 --> 01:14:18.825
In any case, there was
no second time.

980
01:14:19.149 --> 01:14:22.139
- That's what I wanted to tell you.
- What for?

981
01:14:22.453 --> 01:14:23.598
For nothing.

982
01:14:23.940 --> 01:14:25.076
For myself.

983
01:14:27.016 --> 01:14:28.119
I'll go now.

984
01:14:28.809 --> 01:14:31.712
You didn't even touch your gin.
Have a taste.

985
01:14:32.437 --> 01:14:33.818
Don't mind him.

986
01:14:33.915 --> 01:14:34.736
<i>Yes.</i>

987
01:14:34.737 --> 01:14:38.932
Sir, I'm sorry to disturb you at this
hour, but I thought you'd want to know.

988
01:14:39.635 --> 01:14:41.331
It's about the button.

989
01:14:41.541 --> 01:14:43.482
I finally found a lead.

990
01:14:43.691 --> 01:14:45.685
Yes, a suit that matches.

991
01:14:46.279 --> 01:14:48.814
At Lavigne.
Rue Saint-André des Arts.

992
01:14:49.243 --> 01:14:51.130
The sale goes back...

993
01:14:51.795 --> 01:14:52.844
3 years.

994
01:14:54.357 --> 01:14:56.612
No, unfortunately,
they don't know to whom.

995
01:14:56.726 --> 01:14:59.461
A walk-in customer...
But we're searching.

996
01:14:59.462 --> 01:15:02.801
That's it. Keep searching.
When we get that customer's name,

997
01:15:02.802 --> 01:15:05.144
Coméliau will only need
to sign the warrant.

998
01:15:05.249 --> 01:15:08.457
Yes, you're on the right track.
Got it. Thanks.

999
01:15:11.964 --> 01:15:14.586
That was your friend, Detective Lagrume.

1000
01:15:15.758 --> 01:15:18.904
Goodbye, Inspector.
Maybe we'll see other again soon.

1001
01:15:19.061 --> 01:15:20.304
You never know.

1002
01:15:21.343 --> 01:15:24.962
I have no more secrets from you.
But our house has never had any.

1003
01:15:25.067 --> 01:15:26.938
Come whenever you'd like.

1004
01:15:27.235 --> 01:15:29.351
No need to forget your pipe.

1005
01:15:29.500 --> 01:15:33.669
- I'll show you out. - I must run. I'm
meeting my husband at the cinema at 10.

1006
01:15:56.806 --> 01:15:59.410
This is how I noticed.
Do you see it?

1007
01:15:59.787 --> 01:16:00.836
And how.

1008
01:16:01.396 --> 01:16:03.669
I've never seen such sloppy work.

1009
01:16:03.896 --> 01:16:07.830
It's not that hard to open these doors.
Will a little bit of know-how...

1010
01:16:09.665 --> 01:16:11.186
Ah, Inspector.

1011
01:16:13.115 --> 01:16:15.317
Are you coming to see us?
Perfect timing.

1012
01:16:15.422 --> 01:16:17.678
- What happened?
- A burglary.

1013
01:16:17.817 --> 01:16:20.948
- No!
- Deputy Detective Monclare, of the 16th.

1014
01:16:21.140 --> 01:16:23.211
- When?
- We noticed when we got home

1015
01:16:23.212 --> 01:16:24.856
from the cinema, around 12:30.

1016
01:16:24.961 --> 01:16:28.090
If you'd like to take a look, sir,
it's worth it.

1017
01:16:28.528 --> 01:16:29.997
You weren't there?

1018
01:16:30.154 --> 01:16:32.987
- It was my day off.
- See what happens?

1019
01:16:33.196 --> 01:16:36.090
- Do you know what's been taken?
- Not yet.

1020
01:16:36.369 --> 01:16:39.499
Nothing from here. My wife took
a quick inventory.

1021
01:16:39.818 --> 01:16:42.572
- The bedrooms?
- In any case, they didn't touch my jewelry.

1022
01:16:42.694 --> 01:16:45.176
I'm telling you, amateurs, greenhorns.

1023
01:16:45.448 --> 01:16:47.363
We're bound to nick them
on a future job.

1024
01:16:47.485 --> 01:16:48.814
Take a look there.

1025
01:16:48.892 --> 01:16:51.253
Work like that won't get you far.

1026
01:16:51.918 --> 01:16:54.050
- And there?
- That's my bedroom.

1027
01:16:54.234 --> 01:16:55.406
May I?

1028
01:17:04.439 --> 01:17:06.703
- Had you seen that?
- No, I...

1029
01:17:06.842 --> 01:17:09.675
- Well, you'd better have a look.
- Yes.

1030
01:17:12.551 --> 01:17:14.964
At first glance,
there's nothing amiss.

1031
01:17:15.069 --> 01:17:16.136
Say...

1032
01:17:16.773 --> 01:17:18.775
Wait. You did have 6 suits?

1033
01:17:19.125 --> 01:17:20.943
- Yes.
- Well...

1034
01:17:21.118 --> 01:17:24.545
Let's see. The one I wore last night
is in my bedroom...

1035
01:17:26.154 --> 01:17:27.395
Well, I'll be!

1036
01:17:28.301 --> 01:17:29.839
Yvonne darling...

1037
01:17:31.605 --> 01:17:34.595
- Did you send one of my suits
to the cleaner? - No.

1038
01:17:34.804 --> 01:17:38.441
- Well, they stole one of my suits.
- You think so? - Yup.

1039
01:17:40.576 --> 01:17:42.027
One of them is gone!

1040
01:17:42.770 --> 01:17:45.501
Suits mean clothes which mean wardrobe.

1041
01:17:45.607 --> 01:17:47.814
In that case,
you're without sheets or shirts.

1042
01:17:47.928 --> 01:17:50.131
- There are specialists.
- You're scaring me.

1043
01:17:50.236 --> 01:17:53.768
Specialists, I tell you.
5 arrested, just in the past month.

1044
01:17:54.543 --> 01:17:57.620
Breaking into someone's home
to steal a suit. That's too much!

1045
01:17:57.725 --> 01:18:00.365
- Don't you think it looks like a prank?
- I do.

1046
01:18:00.671 --> 01:18:04.570
- I think I should check my bedroom.
- I was about to advise as much.

1047
01:18:06.266 --> 01:18:08.574
Count carefully.
How many did you have?

1048
01:18:08.714 --> 01:18:11.617
I don't know exactly.
There are some at the laundry.

1049
01:18:12.569 --> 01:18:14.107
Count anyway.

1050
01:18:15.340 --> 01:18:16.853
Nothing's missing.

1051
01:18:18.951 --> 01:18:20.489
Not here either.

1052
01:18:20.734 --> 01:18:22.255
They didn't take anything.

1053
01:18:22.359 --> 01:18:25.245
And your household linen?
Check your household linen!

1054
01:18:25.346 --> 01:18:28.406
The sheets! Count them!
They like sheets.

1055
01:18:46.104 --> 01:18:48.203
6, 8, 10, 12...

1056
01:18:49.479 --> 01:18:50.528
Yvonne!

1057
01:18:50.956 --> 01:18:54.033
Come take a look.
I think I'm missing some shirts.

1058
01:18:54.173 --> 01:18:56.307
Shirts! Didn't I say that?

1059
01:19:14.729 --> 01:19:16.863
- Is Georges Vacher in?
- No.

1060
01:19:17.685 --> 01:19:20.866
- He's not alone?
- He asked not to be disturbed.

1061
01:19:21.794 --> 01:19:22.773
Is he alone?

1062
01:19:23.603 --> 01:19:25.631
I think so.
He had a visitor.

1063
01:19:26.147 --> 01:19:29.863
- She came back down a half hour ago.
- What type?

1064
01:19:30.317 --> 01:19:33.088
Mid twenties, brunette,
rather distinguished.

1065
01:19:33.211 --> 01:19:34.260
OK.

1066
01:19:46.263 --> 01:19:48.466
You have luggage?
Shall I call a taxi?

1067
01:19:48.570 --> 01:19:50.704
I'm not doing anything wrong.
I'm off on vacation.

1068
01:19:50.809 --> 01:19:51.980
Lucky you.

1069
01:19:52.609 --> 01:19:55.232
Tell me what Mme Maurin asked you.

1070
01:19:55.625 --> 01:19:57.235
Quickly. I'm in a hurry.

1071
01:19:57.339 --> 01:20:00.137
- So am I. I have a plane to catch.
- Oh yeah?

1072
01:20:00.241 --> 01:20:03.432
I haven't seen that lady since the other
night. So if it's all the same to you...

1073
01:20:03.537 --> 01:20:05.626
Drop your suitcase, would you?

1074
01:20:06.850 --> 01:20:10.102
- Tell me what she came to ask you.
- Nothing, I tell you.

1075
01:20:10.655 --> 01:20:13.767
You have a good head, dear fellow,
but be careful.

1076
01:20:13.872 --> 01:20:16.730
- Why do you say that?
- Because it could get cut off.

1077
01:20:16.836 --> 01:20:19.292
Your discretion is that
of a gentleman, bravo,

1078
01:20:19.397 --> 01:20:22.282
But it could get you charged
with being an accomplice.

1079
01:20:22.387 --> 01:20:24.135
This is a criminal matter.

1080
01:20:25.053 --> 01:20:29.232
With your rap sheet, you might just get
time if you're lucky. But if you're not...

1081
01:20:30.561 --> 01:20:32.081
it's your noggin.

1082
01:20:32.222 --> 01:20:33.078
Your move.

1083
01:20:33.079 --> 01:20:34.651
Playing black or white?

1084
01:20:38.492 --> 01:20:39.523
So...

1085
01:20:39.978 --> 01:20:42.041
Did she arrange
this little getaway?

1086
01:20:42.390 --> 01:20:44.803
Oh, I'm too stupid...

1087
01:20:46.324 --> 01:20:48.939
What the hell do I care?
Yes, she did.

1088
01:20:50.092 --> 01:20:51.125
Here.

1089
01:20:53.118 --> 01:20:56.002
She gave this to me for expenses.
A family jewel.

1090
01:20:57.637 --> 01:20:59.892
Apparently it's worth two grand.

1091
01:21:00.067 --> 01:21:02.323
I would have spent it in the south.

1092
01:21:02.743 --> 01:21:04.526
You're confiscating it?

1093
01:21:04.849 --> 01:21:09.028
What do I have to do with any crimes?
First I'm questioned. Now I'm robbed.

1094
01:21:09.605 --> 01:21:13.101
- I'd really like to know.
- I'll tell you, and with flowers.

1095
01:21:14.666 --> 01:21:17.201
They gave these out
at your club on May 1st.

1096
01:21:18.029 --> 01:21:20.670
When did Mme Maurin first come here?

1097
01:21:21.789 --> 01:21:23.852
Think. Make an effort.

1098
01:21:24.945 --> 01:21:27.620
- It wasn't May 1st?
- Maybe.

1099
01:21:28.249 --> 01:21:31.064
- It's possible... Yes, I think so.
- And I'm sure.

1100
01:21:32.026 --> 01:21:34.684
Why did she want you to leave?
What's between you?

1101
01:21:34.884 --> 01:21:38.487
Not much. She wants me to leave because
her husband knows.

1102
01:21:38.854 --> 01:21:42.753
Supposedly, he wants to come find me.
She takes it easy on her cuckold.

1103
01:21:43.356 --> 01:21:45.821
He cheats on her too.
Has she told you?

1104
01:21:46.258 --> 01:21:49.493
Well, if she had told me that,
I would have had a laugh.

1105
01:21:50.349 --> 01:21:53.252
If that guy does no more harm
to the others than he does to her...

1106
01:21:53.331 --> 01:21:55.464
we'll soon be drowning in chaste women.

1107
01:21:55.569 --> 01:21:58.882
No, I'd rather keep quiet. I don't want
to compromise a young maiden.

1108
01:21:58.986 --> 01:21:59.799
Maiden?

1109
01:22:00.362 --> 01:22:01.761
Do you need a picture?

1110
01:22:04.173 --> 01:22:06.586
Don't speak idly.
Be very careful.

1111
01:22:06.691 --> 01:22:09.051
This "maiden" as you say
has been married for 6 years.

1112
01:22:09.157 --> 01:22:12.836
- You know what that means?
- It's possible she spoke her vows.

1113
01:22:13.169 --> 01:22:15.581
But that's all she did.

1114
01:22:15.782 --> 01:22:18.213
- You can trust me.
- On that, yes.

1115
01:22:18.414 --> 01:22:22.592
She can keep thinking her husband is a
demigod whose shoes I'm not fit to shine.

1116
01:22:22.715 --> 01:22:26.806
That doesn't change the fact that May 1st
from 5 to 7 was her wedding night.

1117
01:22:26.947 --> 01:22:29.499
What bothers her is that I noticed.

1118
01:22:30.250 --> 01:22:31.283
Lucas.

1119
01:22:32.314 --> 01:22:34.336
It's even going very well.

1120
01:22:34.511 --> 01:22:38.690
Go with Torrence to Quai Blériot. I want
the Maurins in my office within the hour.

1121
01:22:40.552 --> 01:22:43.472
You can say there's news!
Does May 1st ring a bell?

1122
01:22:44.276 --> 01:22:48.441
Er, I don't know. May Day, lilies,
rolls in the hay. Am I missing anything?

1123
01:22:49.320 --> 01:22:52.660
Oh, not much.
It's also the day of the first murder.

1124
01:23:07.587 --> 01:23:10.787
- Do you think it'll be much longer?
- I don't know.

1125
01:23:12.430 --> 01:23:15.280
It's almost 9.
For an urgent convocation...

1126
01:23:18.872 --> 01:23:22.893
The inspector is sorry to keep you
waiting. His meeting will end shortly.

1127
01:23:23.278 --> 01:23:25.900
Why were we summoned?
Do you know?

1128
01:23:26.180 --> 01:23:28.995
Let's see.
Weren't you burglarized?

1129
01:23:29.810 --> 01:23:31.471
I think it's why.

1130
01:23:32.136 --> 01:23:35.230
M. Maurin,
could you kindly come this way?

1131
01:23:35.580 --> 01:23:38.168
Just an identification formality.

1132
01:23:39.330 --> 01:23:41.393
No, no, that's not necessary.

1133
01:23:41.507 --> 01:23:44.921
The head of the household's identity
is enough. This way.

1134
01:23:55.484 --> 01:23:57.075
You asked for me, boss?

1135
01:23:57.662 --> 01:24:01.630
Lucas is with Maurin, singing the song.
Go relieve him for the second verse.

1136
01:24:02.005 --> 01:24:05.100
- If your wife is waiting, let her know.
- Will it be long? Because...

1137
01:24:05.239 --> 01:24:08.876
- she was making a soufflé.
- Ah, it's liable to fall back down.

1138
01:24:09.366 --> 01:24:11.796
This chair's a little worn out.

1139
01:24:12.758 --> 01:24:16.395
It's like me. But a lot of suspects
have confessed sitting there.

1140
01:24:16.621 --> 01:24:18.159
Go ahead and laugh.

1141
01:24:18.265 --> 01:24:21.639
You'll see when you have 20 years in.
You'll have your little quirks too.

1142
01:24:21.900 --> 01:24:24.287
First and last names of your father.

1143
01:24:24.392 --> 01:24:27.898
Maurin. Albert, Emile and Lucien.

1144
01:24:37.821 --> 01:24:39.936
- Profession.
- Butcher.

1145
01:24:43.875 --> 01:24:45.955
- Place of birth.
- Paris.

1146
01:24:46.461 --> 01:24:48.123
I forget the district.

1147
01:24:49.907 --> 01:24:51.480
I'll leave it blank.

1148
01:24:52.888 --> 01:24:55.492
You were born in which district?

1149
01:24:55.948 --> 01:24:58.588
- I think I've already told you.
- Oh.

1150
01:24:58.990 --> 01:25:01.420
Yes, you're right. The 4th district.

1151
01:25:02.504 --> 01:25:03.990
Your profession is...

1152
01:25:04.261 --> 01:25:06.533
You're urgently needed at booking.

1153
01:25:07.827 --> 01:25:10.398
It's always when... Excuse me.

1154
01:25:11.115 --> 01:25:14.428
Okay, take my place. No sense in
keeping the gentleman waiting.

1155
01:25:14.524 --> 01:25:17.094
Let's see... Maurin...
OK.

1156
01:25:18.466 --> 01:25:20.546
- These are your papers.
- Yes.

1157
01:25:20.634 --> 01:25:23.974
Maurin. Marcel, Xavier, Raymond.
Born in Paris.

1158
01:25:24.078 --> 01:25:25.616
Which district?

1159
01:25:25.809 --> 01:25:28.729
The 4th.
Your colleague already took it down.

1160
01:25:28.981 --> 01:25:32.357
Maurin. Albert, Emile, Lucien.
Butcher. Born in...

1161
01:25:32.479 --> 01:25:35.399
- There's no district.
- I've forgotten which!

1162
01:25:35.521 --> 01:25:38.283
- No matter.
- Will M. Maigret see us or not?

1163
01:25:38.423 --> 01:25:41.526
Since he asked you to come,
it surely won't be long.

1164
01:25:41.815 --> 01:25:44.665
Well, then, we'll leave
the district blank.

1165
01:25:45.836 --> 01:25:47.934
Your mother's maiden name?

1166
01:25:52.000 --> 01:25:53.573
You find this funny?

1167
01:25:55.042 --> 01:25:56.109
Gauthier.

1168
01:25:57.455 --> 01:25:59.028
Adèle Gauthier.

1169
01:26:00.017 --> 01:26:02.622
First names, birthplace, profession.

1170
01:26:03.356 --> 01:26:04.405
<i>Janvier</i>

1171
01:26:05.157 --> 01:26:07.412
<i>Would you send in Mme Maurin?</i>

1172
01:26:07.815 --> 01:26:08.864
Very well.

1173
01:26:09.100 --> 01:26:11.670
You see?
You didn't wait too long.

1174
01:26:15.831 --> 01:26:18.034
I am sorry to have kept you waiting.

1175
01:26:20.424 --> 01:26:21.491
Please.

1176
01:26:24.673 --> 01:26:25.950
Tell me...

1177
01:26:26.719 --> 01:26:29.237
It's not nice to keep secrets from me.

1178
01:26:29.372 --> 01:26:30.789
Your husband knows all.

1179
01:26:32.694 --> 01:26:33.743
All of what?

1180
01:26:34.058 --> 01:26:37.223
All about your adventures with...
well...

1181
01:26:38.184 --> 01:26:39.268
with Jojo.

1182
01:26:40.089 --> 01:26:41.086
Yes.

1183
01:26:41.383 --> 01:26:43.953
That must have been hard for him.

1184
01:26:44.827 --> 01:26:46.033
Rather, yes.

1185
01:26:46.933 --> 01:26:49.731
And he wasn't touched by your
change of mind?

1186
01:26:49.836 --> 01:26:51.532
I mean, the second time.

1187
01:26:51.654 --> 01:26:55.081
I hope you told him that you left
as you had arrived.

1188
01:26:55.528 --> 01:26:56.595
Of course.

1189
01:26:57.696 --> 01:27:00.003
It seems to me that
in his place...

1190
01:27:00.493 --> 01:27:02.067
It's true that...

1191
01:27:02.732 --> 01:27:04.164
there was May 1st.

1192
01:27:04.269 --> 01:27:05.599
And <i>that</i>...

1193
01:27:05.834 --> 01:27:08.649
Because it was May 1st
that you met this...

1194
01:27:08.807 --> 01:27:09.873
this Jojo.

1195
01:27:10.677 --> 01:27:12.671
- I admit that...
- It was.

1196
01:27:13.615 --> 01:27:15.206
It was May 1st.

1197
01:27:17.110 --> 01:27:19.382
- It's possible.
- It's certain.

1198
01:27:19.855 --> 01:27:21.953
Really, just between us...

1199
01:27:22.111 --> 01:27:24.540
your husband doesn't have that
many reasons to be jealous,

1200
01:27:24.637 --> 01:27:26.158
let alone the right.

1201
01:27:28.424 --> 01:27:30.749
The more philandering men are, the less
they like to be at the receiving end.

1202
01:27:31.117 --> 01:27:32.113
Philandering?

1203
01:27:33.363 --> 01:27:34.447
Oh, yeah.

1204
01:27:34.587 --> 01:27:35.758
His mistress.

1205
01:27:35.881 --> 01:27:37.420
His mistress<i>es</i>.

1206
01:27:37.979 --> 01:27:42.158
In spite of his mistresses and all, he
still had a violent reaction on May 1st.

1207
01:27:42.874 --> 01:27:44.614
He didn't know that day.

1208
01:27:45.139 --> 01:27:47.727
Oh, I thought.
And when did he find out?

1209
01:27:47.831 --> 01:27:49.493
Day before yesterday

1210
01:27:49.929 --> 01:27:53.855
by calling some friends I had supposedly
spent the evening with.

1211
01:27:53.959 --> 01:27:56.494
So you only had it out with him
day before yesterday

1212
01:27:56.564 --> 01:28:00.130
and that's when he found out
about your visiting Rue Etoile.

1213
01:28:00.200 --> 01:28:00.680
Yes.

1214
01:28:00.750 --> 01:28:02.674
Including on May 1st.

1215
01:28:02.778 --> 01:28:03.358
Yes.

1216
01:28:04.355 --> 01:28:06.453
As long as you were talking

1217
01:28:06.750 --> 01:28:08.856
might as well admit everything.

1218
01:28:10.709 --> 01:28:11.689
Is that it?

1219
01:28:12.415 --> 01:28:13.044
Yes.

1220
01:28:14.215 --> 01:28:16.838
Don't you think it's about time
you told the truth?

1221
01:28:17.188 --> 01:28:19.050
- To me.
- I did tell you.

1222
01:28:19.137 --> 01:28:20.379
You know you did not.

1223
01:28:20.484 --> 01:28:21.988
What do you mean?

1224
01:28:22.338 --> 01:28:23.789
I even came on my own to see you...

1225
01:28:23.790 --> 01:28:26.786
You came to see me all right.
But only to tell me tales.

1226
01:28:26.891 --> 01:28:29.784
Your husband has never had a mistress.
You know better than I he's incapable.

1227
01:28:29.881 --> 01:28:31.770
He's not even capable
of being a husband.

1228
01:28:31.874 --> 01:28:34.872
Otherwise, you wouldn't have
sought out a... a Jojo.

1229
01:28:35.306 --> 01:28:36.949
Your heart wasn't even in it.

1230
01:28:37.097 --> 01:28:38.845
You took years to decide.

1231
01:28:38.968 --> 01:28:41.263
You didn't take a lover.
You followed a random man.

1232
01:28:41.371 --> 01:28:44.273
- That's despicable.
- On the contrary. You love your husband.

1233
01:28:44.422 --> 01:28:47.377
A Jojo has no importance.
But let's be clear:

1234
01:28:47.447 --> 01:28:51.049
I'm not talking about the second time.
That was just a red herring.

1235
01:28:51.197 --> 01:28:54.109
You went back to Rue Etoile
because you were being followed.

1236
01:28:54.205 --> 01:28:56.469
You didn't want to lead my detective
to Quai Blériot.

1237
01:28:56.574 --> 01:28:57.833
You were afraid.

1238
01:28:57.937 --> 01:28:59.161
Afraid of what?

1239
01:29:03.436 --> 01:29:05.446
What happened on May 1st?

1240
01:29:05.586 --> 01:29:07.422
Don't you think
it's time to tell me?

1241
01:29:07.527 --> 01:29:10.481
- I've told you ten times. - I'm not
asking what happened from 5 to 7.

1242
01:29:10.586 --> 01:29:13.716
I'm asking what happened afterwards?
That same night.

1243
01:29:14.948 --> 01:29:18.078
Come on, tell the truth.
I'm saying this for your sake.

1244
01:29:18.488 --> 01:29:21.287
That's why I saw you first.
I'll know the truth sooner or later.

1245
01:29:21.391 --> 01:29:23.734
Perhaps you alone can make it...

1246
01:29:25.691 --> 01:29:26.951
palatable.

1247
01:29:27.930 --> 01:29:29.538
Do you understand?

1248
01:29:30.378 --> 01:29:32.458
I have nothing to say to you.

1249
01:29:34.312 --> 01:29:36.392
Think carefully.

1250
01:29:36.777 --> 01:29:38.333
It's useless.

1251
01:29:41.383 --> 01:29:43.464
Then leave. You're free to go.

1252
01:29:54.443 --> 01:29:57.047
What about my husband?
Will it be long?

1253
01:29:57.161 --> 01:29:59.243
The time it takes him
to answer my questions.

1254
01:29:59.356 --> 01:30:02.739
- Questions of the same sort as...
- Of whatever sort I wish.

1255
01:30:07.546 --> 01:30:10.624
So. We were saying
Marcel Xavier Emile.

1256
01:30:12.862 --> 01:30:14.383
Was that it?

1257
01:30:14.767 --> 01:30:15.816
Yes.

1258
01:30:20.371 --> 01:30:21.542
Oh no!

1259
01:30:22.093 --> 01:30:25.747
Look what you made me do.
Emile, that's your <i>father's</i> first name!

1260
01:30:26.289 --> 01:30:28.895
You, you're Marcel Xavier Raymond! Eh?

1261
01:30:31.021 --> 01:30:34.448
- You don't your own name anymore?
- Of course! I made a mistake.

1262
01:30:34.693 --> 01:30:38.662
OK, but I have to ask to be more careful.
Because of the corrections, you see.

1263
01:30:38.776 --> 01:30:41.905
So we were saying Marcel Xavier Raymond.

1264
01:30:42.779 --> 01:30:43.496
Yes.

1265
01:30:43.801 --> 01:30:47.535
M. Maurin. Please come with me.
The Inspector is ready to see you.

1266
01:30:50.979 --> 01:30:52.570
That was quick.

1267
01:30:58.140 --> 01:31:01.271
Tell Paul to bring up
some sandwiches and some beer.

1268
01:31:03.368 --> 01:31:04.417
5 or 6.

1269
01:31:09.584 --> 01:31:11.139
Come in, M. Maurin.

1270
01:31:12.696 --> 01:31:13.745
Sit down.

1271
01:31:14.829 --> 01:31:18.238
I'm sorry I kept you waiting.
I have some good news.

1272
01:31:18.912 --> 01:31:21.517
I think we found your burglars.

1273
01:31:22.444 --> 01:31:24.227
And we recovered this.

1274
01:31:26.622 --> 01:31:27.986
Isn't it yours?

1275
01:31:28.432 --> 01:31:29.743
My wife's, yes.

1276
01:31:30.023 --> 01:31:34.201
I thought so... You know what? Just
between us, I don't think she noticed.

1277
01:31:34.936 --> 01:31:38.555
- In her panic, she must have...
- The important thing is we found it.

1278
01:31:39.009 --> 01:31:42.140
OK. You need to sign a release.
Here.

1279
01:31:43.424 --> 01:31:44.473
Excuse me.

1280
01:31:49.663 --> 01:31:50.816
Thank you.

1281
01:31:52.381 --> 01:31:55.668
Those are strange ducks.
Have you heard the latest?

1282
01:31:56.084 --> 01:31:59.003
They absolutely deny
having stolen your suit.

1283
01:31:59.737 --> 01:32:02.378
I'm sure they'll eventually confess
and we'll find it. Still...

1284
01:32:02.552 --> 01:32:05.665
By the way,
in case we need to identify this suit...

1285
01:32:05.769 --> 01:32:08.025
It does come from
Bernheim & Son, eh?

1286
01:32:08.130 --> 01:32:09.511
No, in fact...

1287
01:32:09.826 --> 01:32:11.399
It was an old suit.

1288
01:32:13.011 --> 01:32:15.826
Back then, I got clothes
from everywhere, so...

1289
01:32:15.932 --> 01:32:17.978
I don't remember where...

1290
01:32:18.450 --> 01:32:21.561
A store like...
Cygran, Madelios, Albar,

1291
01:32:22.969 --> 01:32:24.350
... Lavigne?

1292
01:32:24.953 --> 01:32:26.649
Yes, that kind.

1293
01:32:26.771 --> 01:32:28.834
Let's go with Lavigne.

1294
01:32:29.586 --> 01:32:31.439
With a question mark, eh?

1295
01:32:33.205 --> 01:32:34.063
Yes.

1296
01:32:34.064 --> 01:32:35.522
That's too complicated.

1297
01:32:35.523 --> 01:32:36.894
No question mark.

1298
01:32:36.990 --> 01:32:39.717
It's late.
I don't want to keep you any longer.

1299
01:32:39.840 --> 01:32:42.960
We'll write it all down.
And we'll get out of here.

1300
01:32:44.027 --> 01:32:47.157
- My wife will wonder...
- Oh I forgot. One moment.

1301
01:32:50.967 --> 01:32:52.174
Janvier?

1302
01:32:52.296 --> 01:32:55.425
Tell Mme Maurin we'll be
another 15 minutes or so

1303
01:32:59.370 --> 01:33:00.961
She already left.

1304
01:33:01.451 --> 01:33:03.531
She probably got tired of waiting.

1305
01:33:03.759 --> 01:33:05.542
Send Lucas in.

1306
01:33:06.582 --> 01:33:10.743
That way, your statement will be in order,
and we won't need to revisit it.

1307
01:33:14.494 --> 01:33:17.623
Your initials in the margin,
and your signature here.

1308
01:33:25.817 --> 01:33:27.390
Glad that's done.

1309
01:33:27.932 --> 01:33:29.488
Yes, come in!

1310
01:33:30.573 --> 01:33:31.796
Finally!

1311
01:33:32.478 --> 01:33:34.803
I thought you'd forgotten about me.

1312
01:33:34.926 --> 01:33:36.465
Put it down here.

1313
01:33:39.239 --> 01:33:42.072
- I'll leave my bottle opener.
- Thank you.

1314
01:33:42.526 --> 01:33:46.180
- Will you have a beer?
- Thank you. I don't drink alcohol.

1315
01:33:46.635 --> 01:33:49.887
You don't smoke. You don't drink.
So you have no vice.

1316
01:33:51.115 --> 01:33:52.671
I have them all.

1317
01:33:53.230 --> 01:33:56.552
- How about a sandwich.
- I don't eat between meals.

1318
01:33:57.462 --> 01:34:01.623
This isn't between meals. It's the meal.
It's almost 10, and we're not done.

1319
01:34:02.016 --> 01:34:06.186
If you're not feeling well, make yourself
comfortable. No formalities between us.

1320
01:34:09.447 --> 01:34:12.770
While you're here, I have a little
clarification to ask you about.

1321
01:34:12.882 --> 01:34:16.851
- I'm worried my wife will...
- Right, sorry. So give her a call.

1322
01:34:18.680 --> 01:34:20.254
Excuse me, boss.

1323
01:34:21.521 --> 01:34:23.513
I have this request here.

1324
01:34:24.160 --> 01:34:25.751
What should I do with it?

1325
01:34:25.752 --> 01:34:27.290
<i>The mother is here.</i>

1326
01:34:28.575 --> 01:34:30.988
Keep it on file.
I might need it.

1327
01:34:33.952 --> 01:34:35.316
Yes, it's me.

1328
01:34:36.409 --> 01:34:37.999
Yes, I'm still there.

1329
01:34:39.608 --> 01:34:41.689
But it's about our burglary.

1330
01:34:44.154 --> 01:34:45.955
Oh, we'll be another...

1331
01:34:46.837 --> 01:34:48.410
a... a little while.

1332
01:34:50.106 --> 01:34:51.662
No, not at all.

1333
01:34:53.568 --> 01:34:55.142
Right. See you soon.

1334
01:34:57.688 --> 01:35:01.307
You didn't tell her about the brooch.
She would have liked that.

1335
01:35:01.586 --> 01:35:03.668
Oh, you want to surprise her!

1336
01:35:09.586 --> 01:35:11.246
So where was I?

1337
01:35:13.100 --> 01:35:15.128
You had a little clarification
to ask me.

1338
01:35:15.984 --> 01:35:19.464
It's about Barberot again.
That guy is still bothering me.

1339
01:35:19.728 --> 01:35:21.668
I can't get him to admit he knows

1340
01:35:21.669 --> 01:35:24.264
- about that small door.
- Small door?

1341
01:35:24.492 --> 01:35:27.692
Yes, the one at No. 22, that leads to
the cul-de-sac, next to the trash...

1342
01:35:27.788 --> 01:35:29.379
you know, the little door!

1343
01:35:31.319 --> 01:35:33.925
Don't tell me you don't know it either.

1344
01:35:34.449 --> 01:35:37.474
You must know it.
You were born in that building.

1345
01:35:37.649 --> 01:35:41.818
You'd pass through it to go play in the
courtyards. Like all the other kids.

1346
01:35:42.019 --> 01:35:44.135
Above all, your mom didn't like that.

1347
01:35:44.257 --> 01:35:46.863
So, you'd go through there.
Sight unseen.

1348
01:35:47.667 --> 01:35:50.010
We've all done it.
There's no harm.

1349
01:35:51.401 --> 01:35:52.397
Yes...

1350
01:35:52.747 --> 01:35:55.020
- I must have known about it.
- Of course.

1351
01:35:55.124 --> 01:35:57.835
- But I didn't use it.
- I'm sure not.

1352
01:35:58.341 --> 01:36:00.055
I'll even tell you why.

1353
01:36:00.554 --> 01:36:03.211
It should have had the lure of the
forbidden fruit.

1354
01:36:03.316 --> 01:36:06.918
But it had no interest for you. Too easy.
Given that your mother had the key.

1355
01:36:10.152 --> 01:36:11.726
She did have the key?

1356
01:36:13.002 --> 01:36:14.400
It's possible, yes.

1357
01:36:14.505 --> 01:36:16.971
Yet she claims not to.
I wonder why.

1358
01:36:17.154 --> 01:36:18.815
You must wonder, too.

1359
01:36:19.095 --> 01:36:22.294
What if we asked her?
We'll clear this up for good.

1360
01:36:22.390 --> 01:36:23.597
Send in Mme Maurin.

1361
01:36:23.947 --> 01:36:27.076
- My mother's here?
- Yes. I don't even know why.

1362
01:36:30.724 --> 01:36:34.379
Marcel, darling, don't be afraid anymore.
Your mother is here.

1363
01:36:34.947 --> 01:36:38.339
- What do you want with him? What are
you doing to him? -  Nothing, mom!

1364
01:36:38.444 --> 01:36:42.420
Just chatting. Your son confirmed you had
the key to the little door downstairs.

1365
01:36:42.526 --> 01:36:46.696
- I confirmed no such thing.
- Why have you always insisted otherwise?

1366
01:36:46.941 --> 01:36:50.140
I know it's of no importance to you,
but... Please, have a seat.

1367
01:36:50.464 --> 01:36:54.171
No need. I have no intention of staying.
I came to get my son. Do you hear?

1368
01:36:54.294 --> 01:36:57.423
Don't let him intimidate you!
Let's go. Come on!

1369
01:36:57.887 --> 01:36:59.268
They won't dare hold you.

1370
01:36:59.600 --> 01:37:01.314
I'm afraid we dare.

1371
01:37:01.315 --> 01:37:03.429
If my son is under arrest, say so!

1372
01:37:03.552 --> 01:37:06.472
I'll call our lawyer immediately.
M. Liotard.

1373
01:37:06.690 --> 01:37:10.116
- You must know M. Liotard.
- Very well. A fine mouthpiece.

1374
01:37:10.221 --> 01:37:13.442
- Well, you'll explain yourself with him!
- Calm down, mom.

1375
01:37:13.582 --> 01:37:15.348
I don't need a lawyer!

1376
01:37:15.452 --> 01:37:18.057
Absolutely not! He's right.
Calm down, Madame.

1377
01:37:18.163 --> 01:37:21.913
- I just asked him about the little door...
- I don't have to answer it!

1378
01:37:22.035 --> 01:37:25.419
Not that question or any others. I will
answer nothing. You too, Marcel.

1379
01:37:25.523 --> 01:37:27.219
You have no business here.

1380
01:37:27.323 --> 01:37:30.278
Since he's holding you,
M. Liotard will get you out.

1381
01:37:30.452 --> 01:37:33.058
And with apologies!
I promise you.

1382
01:37:42.691 --> 01:37:46.083
Your father couldn't have had a lot
of fun every day with her.

1383
01:37:46.707 --> 01:37:49.313
In a way, that explains Mauricette.

1384
01:37:50.156 --> 01:37:51.205
Mauricette...

1385
01:37:51.306 --> 01:37:53.902
Maybe I shouldn't have brought her up.
But still...

1386
01:37:54.007 --> 01:37:56.822
We're talking man to man.
We have to face things.

1387
01:37:56.935 --> 01:38:00.467
Papa Maurin was handy,
and Mauricette was a dish.

1388
01:38:00.590 --> 01:38:02.154
Still is, the bitch.

1389
01:38:03.002 --> 01:38:06.167
When I think about what you went
through 15 years ago...

1390
01:38:07.321 --> 01:38:08.370
Slut...

1391
01:38:08.510 --> 01:38:10.083
I know. You wrote me.

1392
01:38:11.914 --> 01:38:15.638
"No, M. Maigret. The killer of those
sluts in the Marais is not a madman."

1393
01:38:15.744 --> 01:38:18.873
- I didn't write this!
- Oh, come now. Look.

1394
01:38:19.800 --> 01:38:22.055
Razor blade, transfer paper,

1395
01:38:22.545 --> 01:38:26.199
- white glue. That's an artist's work.
It's almost like decor. - No, no!

1396
01:38:26.487 --> 01:38:30.666
Why are you protesting? It's not worth
the bother. Everybody writes us. Here.

1397
01:38:31.496 --> 01:38:33.140
This is full of them.

1398
01:38:33.262 --> 01:38:36.164
Amateur detectives,
readers of crime novels,

1399
01:38:37.371 --> 01:38:39.461
insane people, mediums,

1400
01:38:40.265 --> 01:38:43.359
... or simply practical jokers.
That's your case.

1401
01:38:43.971 --> 01:38:45.921
You're a big child, Maurin.

1402
01:38:46.034 --> 01:38:48.518
You wrote in to make me mad.
Like a game.

1403
01:38:48.622 --> 01:38:51.725
- No, no, no...
- You did. As a game. You did.

1404
01:38:52.765 --> 01:38:56.909
Fits right in with the toy crane and
the water in the miniature fountain.

1405
01:38:57.023 --> 01:39:00.895
Your mother speaks of sensitivity, but...
Me, I call it whimsy.

1406
01:39:01.914 --> 01:39:03.172
Come on.

1407
01:39:03.417 --> 01:39:06.023
This letter smells like a joke, a hoax.

1408
01:39:06.564 --> 01:39:09.781
It's incapable of writing
a denunciation letter, but...

1409
01:39:09.886 --> 01:39:13.339
when it comes to mocking the police,
to crossing the inspector, that's...

1410
01:39:13.444 --> 01:39:17.063
- prime material for a practical joke.
- A little sophomoric humor. - Exactly!

1411
01:39:18.007 --> 01:39:21.146
Did it ever occur to you
this was a punishable offense?

1412
01:39:21.723 --> 01:39:23.838
Well, "Contempt of Law."

1413
01:39:24.162 --> 01:39:26.243
Wait, we'll find it for you.

1414
01:39:26.732 --> 01:39:27.834
Right here.

1415
01:39:29.495 --> 01:39:31.121
Article 222.

1416
01:39:31.575 --> 01:39:34.373
Punishable by 15 days to 1 year of jail.

1417
01:39:34.489 --> 01:39:37.496
Just in case you want to
make yourself mad too. Eh?

1418
01:39:37.706 --> 01:39:40.644
OK. We won't talk about it again.
With anyone.

1419
01:39:40.941 --> 01:39:44.560
Especially since I'm sure that
your wife doesn't know about it.

1420
01:39:44.665 --> 01:39:46.762
Admit that you didn't tell her.

1421
01:39:47.375 --> 01:39:49.455
Come on.
Just between us.

1422
01:39:51.553 --> 01:39:52.348
No.

1423
01:39:53.520 --> 01:39:54.569
You see?

1424
01:39:55.995 --> 01:39:58.075
All this is confidential, ok?

1425
01:39:58.250 --> 01:40:01.117
Ok, as long as you're here...
Write:

1426
01:40:02.778 --> 01:40:04.071
"I admit...

1427
01:40:05.636 --> 01:40:07.210
"... under oath...

1428
01:40:09.098 --> 01:40:10.672
"... that I wrote...

1429
01:40:11.380 --> 01:40:13.810
"... with no harmful intent..."

1430
01:40:16.206 --> 01:40:19.003
- Excuse me, boss. Lagrume.
- In a minute.

1431
01:40:19.134 --> 01:40:20.709
He's insisting.

1432
01:40:20.996 --> 01:40:22.867
OK, carry on.

1433
01:40:23.199 --> 01:40:25.384
You, sign.
And we can go home.

1434
01:40:25.525 --> 01:40:26.835
"I admit..."

1435
01:40:29.597 --> 01:40:32.789
- What is it, Lagrume?
- Sir, I know how precious your time is.

1436
01:40:32.790 --> 01:40:36.102
But I thought it my duty to inform you
as quickly as possible...

1437
01:40:36.198 --> 01:40:38.016
Quickly, man, quickly.

1438
01:40:38.134 --> 01:40:42.295
- I think it's necessary to start at the
beginning. - I'd prefer the ending.

1439
01:40:42.977 --> 01:40:46.300
I do believe I've found the suit
with the button.

1440
01:40:47.025 --> 01:40:48.581
At least, a sample.

1441
01:40:49.665 --> 01:40:50.879
Sold ready-made

1442
01:40:50.880 --> 01:40:51.938
3 years ago

1443
01:40:52.481 --> 01:40:54.613
by Lavigne to a walk-in customer.

1444
01:40:54.850 --> 01:40:59.011
- Whose name you don't know. You told me
on the phone. Is that all? - No.

1445
01:40:59.885 --> 01:41:04.064
While looking through her books back
to 1939, Mme Lavigne, a charming woman,

1446
01:41:04.851 --> 01:41:08.356
found the name of another client
who might perhaps interest you:

1447
01:41:08.513 --> 01:41:10.594
Maurin, Emile.

1448
01:41:11.428 --> 01:41:12.670
The father?

1449
01:41:12.933 --> 01:41:13.982
Yup.

1450
01:41:21.828 --> 01:41:25.097
I must say, M. Maurin, everyone
is looking after you.

1451
01:41:25.255 --> 01:41:28.245
It's Detective Lagrume.
It looks like he found your suit.

1452
01:41:29.259 --> 01:41:32.109
When I say your suit,
I mean, your father's.

1453
01:41:33.932 --> 01:41:36.274
My father's?
That's absurd.

1454
01:41:37.201 --> 01:41:40.277
Your suit that was so-called stolen
came from Lavigne.

1455
01:41:40.365 --> 01:41:42.184
- No, I...
- You told me.

1456
01:41:42.585 --> 01:41:45.907
But you simply forgot to specify
that it wasn't yours.

1457
01:41:47.026 --> 01:41:48.600
Come on, that's absurd.

1458
01:41:48.914 --> 01:41:50.820
I'm telling you, it's absurd.

1459
01:41:51.074 --> 01:41:53.242
One of my father's suits, what for?

1460
01:41:53.382 --> 01:41:55.672
I have mine.
You saw my wardrobe.

1461
01:41:55.838 --> 01:41:59.737
The night of the reconstruction, you went
out wearing a dark Prince of Wales suit.

1462
01:41:59.843 --> 01:42:03.409
Your own suit. No reason not to be frank
with you. Here.

1463
01:42:03.513 --> 01:42:06.136
- A suit like this.
- I've never had a suit like this!

1464
01:42:06.250 --> 01:42:09.274
I don't understand why you're being
so stubborn, M. Maurin.

1465
01:42:09.440 --> 01:42:12.045
Why not just tell me how it happened?

1466
01:42:13.146 --> 01:42:14.719
I'll tell you how.

1467
01:42:15.253 --> 01:42:19.519
That night, after your failed attempt,
you ran panicked, with folks on your tail.

1468
01:42:20.026 --> 01:42:24.012
You cut through the courtyards and went
through, yes, that famous little door.

1469
01:42:24.151 --> 01:42:28.339
- You go up to mother's and she gives you
one of dad's suits. - But why, why, why?

1470
01:42:28.445 --> 01:42:31.206
Because a button has been ripped
from your suit.

1471
01:42:31.302 --> 01:42:32.841
This is nonsense. What button?

1472
01:42:32.946 --> 01:42:34.634
- Here. This one.
- No!

1473
01:42:34.900 --> 01:42:36.404
- No!
- Yes.

1474
01:42:36.543 --> 01:42:40.425
And since you're afraid of being spotted,
you change suits and you go home quietly.

1475
01:42:40.801 --> 01:42:44.962
Come on, talk. You've already said a lot.
So go ahead and unload the rest.

1476
01:42:45.041 --> 01:42:48.433
You'll feel relieved, at peace. You'll
go home to sleep and it'll all be over.

1477
01:42:48.555 --> 01:42:52.751
You feel a need to tell me everything.
You've wanted to for a long time. I know it.

1478
01:42:52.856 --> 01:42:55.462
So talk, man. Come on, talk!

1479
01:42:56.633 --> 01:42:57.891
I want to leave!

1480
01:42:57.892 --> 01:43:00.917
You hear me? I want to go home.
Let me go home!

1481
01:43:01.022 --> 01:43:03.557
Leave me alone!
I want to be left alone!

1482
01:43:03.664 --> 01:43:06.688
I didn't do anything.
I've never done anything.

1483
01:43:07.773 --> 01:43:09.101
You have no right.

1484
01:43:09.363 --> 01:43:10.936
You are monsters.

1485
01:43:25.335 --> 01:43:26.909
Marcel, look at me.

1486
01:43:27.966 --> 01:43:29.575
Come on, look at me.

1487
01:43:29.662 --> 01:43:31.726
Come on, come on.
Like this.

1488
01:43:33.666 --> 01:43:35.904
Listen to me.
Will you listen?

1489
01:43:36.778 --> 01:43:40.432
You don't look like a murderer. I know
murderers. You're not one.

1490
01:43:41.368 --> 01:43:43.982
The thing is, without being a murderer,
well...

1491
01:43:44.244 --> 01:43:47.077
- ... can still lead you to kill.
- I didn't kill!

1492
01:43:47.172 --> 01:43:49.254
Ok, ok. Well...

1493
01:43:49.726 --> 01:43:52.855
Then tell me what happened.
Just me, eh?

1494
01:43:53.275 --> 01:43:55.557
Tell me what they did to you.

1495
01:43:55.661 --> 01:43:57.269
They made you so unhappy?

1496
01:43:57.453 --> 01:44:00.347
I know how you are.
I can put myself in your shoes.

1497
01:44:00.447 --> 01:44:03.961
You must have suffered. I mean, enough to
make yourself sick the night you knew

1498
01:44:04.030 --> 01:44:06.146
that Yvonne was coming back
from that guy's bed.

1499
01:44:07.045 --> 01:44:09.965
Must have been quite a scene
when she came home, eh?

1500
01:44:10.071 --> 01:44:13.148
- It must have been awful for you.
- The slut!

1501
01:44:13.437 --> 01:44:17.195
Of course! You insulted her. You must
have wanted to give her a beating, eh?

1502
01:44:17.339 --> 01:44:20.862
Just like to Mauricette back then.
Because she slapped you, that Mauricette.

1503
01:44:21.124 --> 01:44:22.278
Slut!

1504
01:44:22.864 --> 01:44:24.980
Maybe Yvonne slapped you too.

1505
01:44:25.382 --> 01:44:28.790
But now you weren't the same age.
It hurt more. You were a man!

1506
01:44:28.896 --> 01:44:31.117
Because you <i>are</i> a man.
I know it.

1507
01:44:31.256 --> 01:44:34.849
Only, that's what they haven't understood.
Your wife no more than your mother.

1508
01:44:34.937 --> 01:44:35.846
The slut.

1509
01:44:35.847 --> 01:44:36.890
Of course.

1510
01:44:36.995 --> 01:44:41.192
Poor Marcel, tossed between Rue Turenne
and Quai Blériot. Between your two women.

1511
01:44:43.429 --> 01:44:45.231
Marcel, look at me.

1512
01:44:45.545 --> 01:44:48.482
Look me in the eyes
and tell me if I'm wrong.

1513
01:44:48.867 --> 01:44:51.945
It's not just for revenge against Yvonne.
It's to say no to all those sluts,

1514
01:44:52.049 --> 01:44:55.240
to free yourself, that you went into the
streets on May 1st, and killed that girl.

1515
01:44:55.423 --> 01:44:58.019
No, I didn't kill!
I tell you, I didn't kill!

1516
01:44:58.125 --> 01:45:01.595
You did! I'm sure it brought you relief.
And the proof is, you did it again.

1517
01:45:01.699 --> 01:45:05.702
You liked it, eh? Tearing their clothes,
sullying them. You were settling scores.

1518
01:45:05.808 --> 01:45:07.110
I didn't do it.

1519
01:45:07.389 --> 01:45:08.963
No, I didn't kill.

1520
01:45:09.793 --> 01:45:12.101
I'm telling you, I didn't kill.

1521
01:45:21.990 --> 01:45:23.545
Hello?
Yes.

1522
01:45:26.580 --> 01:45:27.629
What?

1523
01:45:30.208 --> 01:45:31.257
No!

1524
01:45:32.796 --> 01:45:34.351
Just a moment.

1525
01:45:46.865 --> 01:45:48.420
That can't be!

1526
01:45:55.931 --> 01:45:58.011
Call the doctor on duty.

1527
01:45:58.239 --> 01:45:59.812
You, come with me.

1528
01:46:00.284 --> 01:46:01.719
What's going on?

1529
01:46:02.050 --> 01:46:04.602
3 stab wounds,
and a 4th at neck level.

1530
01:46:04.707 --> 01:46:07.138
The shredding might be different.

1531
01:46:07.304 --> 01:46:09.384
It will be difficult to establish.

1532
01:46:10.188 --> 01:46:14.175
Otherwise, she's not brunette or plump.
Struck not in the chest, but in the back.

1533
01:46:14.279 --> 01:46:16.028
Of course, the end result is the same.

1534
01:46:17.834 --> 01:46:21.104
Yet I'm sure it was his suit.
I couldn't be mistaken.

1535
01:46:21.943 --> 01:46:25.859
We could not have both been wrong
from the start, sir. Not both of us.

1536
01:46:27.546 --> 01:46:28.578
The old lady!

1537
01:46:28.875 --> 01:46:32.005
Go get me the old lady.
And bring her in, willingly or not.

1538
01:46:32.109 --> 01:46:33.158
Off you go.

1539
01:46:33.254 --> 01:46:34.355
Hey, Lucas!

1540
01:46:52.699 --> 01:46:53.775
Who's the woman?

1541
01:46:59.465 --> 01:47:01.039
Please take a seat.

1542
01:47:18.745 --> 01:47:21.875
My compliments, your honor.
Your sources work quickly.

1543
01:47:23.545 --> 01:47:25.285
What matters is that you know.

1544
01:47:25.286 --> 01:47:28.406
I do by necessity.
Awakened in the dead of night.

1545
01:47:29.036 --> 01:47:32.908
I'd rather not repeat what the District
Attorney told me. It was charming.

1546
01:47:33.048 --> 01:47:37.218
I was forced to tell him I had signed no
warrant. And would be signing none.

1547
01:47:38.058 --> 01:47:41.406
You'd better release this man within the
hour. Do you hear, my friend? One hour.

1548
01:47:41.407 --> 01:47:43.343
Within a minute, your honor.

1549
01:47:44.749 --> 01:47:47.599
Yes, yes, don't worry.
M. Liotard is here.

1550
01:47:49.226 --> 01:47:51.043
Good night, your honor.

1551
01:47:52.049 --> 01:47:54.251
You heard, counselor.
I'm giving you back your client.

1552
01:47:54.364 --> 01:47:56.944
Take care of him.
I have a feeling we'll need him again.

1553
01:47:57.040 --> 01:47:59.347
Don't you find this irony
somewhat inappropriate?

1554
01:47:59.453 --> 01:48:01.008
Sadly, it's all I have left.

1555
01:48:01.113 --> 01:48:04.243
I'll have him taken home. Unless you find
it more prudent to take him with you.

1556
01:48:04.347 --> 01:48:06.148
As long as I have your word.

1557
01:48:17.080 --> 01:48:20.000
- Is he in shape to go home?
- Yes. - Then, send him home.

1558
01:48:20.603 --> 01:48:22.509
Send someone with him in a taxi.

1559
01:48:22.613 --> 01:48:25.516
Come, M. Maurin. You're going home.
Come on.

1560
01:48:28.156 --> 01:48:30.814
Lapointe, I'd rather
you take the back door.

1561
01:48:30.954 --> 01:48:33.944
Say, he looks a bit shell shocked.
Did you shake him?

1562
01:48:34.048 --> 01:48:38.191
No. Yet we're talking a real half-wit who
could use a couple of smacks, I tell you.

1563
01:48:38.307 --> 01:48:40.544
I have nothing to say. Go, go.

1564
01:48:44.951 --> 01:48:47.521
- They're here.
- Not too much trouble?

1565
01:48:47.643 --> 01:48:50.913
- And when they saw each other?
- No reaction. Like they've never met.

1566
01:49:04.592 --> 01:49:07.769
Well, ladies, you can be happy.
Your darling is free.

1567
01:49:07.874 --> 01:49:10.391
Your baby chick just left.
He can start killing again.

1568
01:49:10.488 --> 01:49:11.030
What?

1569
01:49:11.135 --> 01:49:14.527
Because he's already killed 4 times.
I know it, and so do you!

1570
01:49:15.550 --> 01:49:18.680
The child prodigy. The artist.
4 times!

1571
01:49:19.536 --> 01:49:22.665
- The Marais Killer. That's him.
- But that's nonsense!

1572
01:49:22.771 --> 01:49:24.606
You don't seriously think that,
M. Maigret.

1573
01:49:24.703 --> 01:49:28.077
- This is monstrous, grotesque! I wonder...
- Do you have a confession to make?

1574
01:49:28.183 --> 01:49:31.050
- But that's too much...!
- Then be quiet!

1575
01:49:33.716 --> 01:49:35.290
And you knew it.

1576
01:49:36.481 --> 01:49:40.102
You. You knew it the night you came
to my home. Oh, not for very long...

1577
01:49:40.206 --> 01:49:44.375
- Maybe you'll tell me the exact moment?
- The minute! When I opened the wardrobe.

1578
01:49:44.559 --> 01:49:46.779
Because you instantly spotted
the suit that wasn't his.

1579
01:49:46.883 --> 01:49:49.630
And you knew then that
Marcel had gone out, and where!

1580
01:49:49.734 --> 01:49:50.678
Don't answer!

1581
01:49:51.281 --> 01:49:53.886
You don't have the right to question us
without a lawyer present!

1582
01:49:54.104 --> 01:49:57.496
And you, when you helped him change
suits, you knew it too!

1583
01:49:58.021 --> 01:50:00.468
Neither one of you blinked.
Love is grand.

1584
01:50:00.573 --> 01:50:03.284
- You loved your Marcel.
- I certainly hope so!

1585
01:50:03.406 --> 01:50:05.609
You can be proud, and for cause.

1586
01:50:05.775 --> 01:50:08.783
You were flattered by the "artist" angle.
It comforted you from the father, from...

1587
01:50:08.895 --> 01:50:12.305
from the boor, from the butcher.
Because <i>he</i> had a trade, the poor fool.

1588
01:50:12.418 --> 01:50:14.149
A <i>trade</i>...

1589
01:50:14.515 --> 01:50:16.614
Mme Maurin, you are a monster.

1590
01:50:17.462 --> 01:50:19.631
But above all, a monster of stupidity...

1591
01:50:19.912 --> 01:50:22.774
- You are behaving like...
- ... and vain...

1592
01:50:23.421 --> 01:50:25.580
... possessive, mean-spirited...

1593
01:50:26.000 --> 01:50:29.714
But mostly, you are stupid!
And I mean, stupid!

1594
01:50:29.924 --> 01:50:32.787
Because you stultified your son.
You kept him away from his father,

1595
01:50:32.891 --> 01:50:36.062
from boys his own age, from everything
that could make a boy like others.

1596
01:50:36.150 --> 01:50:40.022
Because he's not like others! And that,
you both know. Ask his wife.

1597
01:50:41.071 --> 01:50:45.243
Marcel might have been gifted. But not
for everything. And that's your handiwork.

1598
01:50:45.636 --> 01:50:49.325
The little violin, the little piano,
the little sonatas...

1599
01:50:49.431 --> 01:50:51.738
mom's portrait, mom's little darling.

1600
01:50:51.834 --> 01:50:55.182
On the eve of his wedding, you probably
still had him sleeping with a teddy bear.

1601
01:50:55.475 --> 01:50:58.447
You buried him in his childhood.
You made him a retard.

1602
01:50:58.561 --> 01:51:00.265
Each in her own way.

1603
01:51:00.667 --> 01:51:03.635
Because then you took the baton.
More adored than ever, that Marcel.

1604
01:51:03.810 --> 01:51:06.476
He no doubt got married to get some
peace, a change of scenery.

1605
01:51:06.581 --> 01:51:08.260
But he only managed to change females.

1606
01:51:08.365 --> 01:51:09.973
Because she took him, your precious.

1607
01:51:09.974 --> 01:51:11.101
With her dowry.

1608
01:51:11.241 --> 01:51:14.213
I'll say! He doesn't spit
on material comfort, the artist.

1609
01:51:14.397 --> 01:51:16.582
He preferred Quai Blériot to Rue Turenne.

1610
01:51:16.714 --> 01:51:20.026
From failed painter, he became a phony
decorator. Hey, when you've got talent...

1611
01:51:20.166 --> 01:51:21.801
Disgraceful! This is disgraceful!

1612
01:51:21.907 --> 01:51:24.757
Admired and fed.
You were the ideal wife.

1613
01:51:24.914 --> 01:51:26.225
A new mom.

1614
01:51:26.522 --> 01:51:30.097
But this one didn't content herself with
tucking him into bed. She slept in it.

1615
01:51:30.202 --> 01:51:31.968
Mom with needs.

1616
01:51:32.072 --> 01:51:34.853
Needs she ended up
going elsewhere to satisfy.

1617
01:51:35.019 --> 01:51:35.788
Whore!

1618
01:51:35.910 --> 01:51:38.096
Dirty little whore!
I'm not surprised.

1619
01:51:38.201 --> 01:51:39.975
Well, the moron was surprised.

1620
01:51:40.079 --> 01:51:43.909
And since he didn't dare kill her, he
made up for it on others. The poor girls.

1621
01:51:44.512 --> 01:51:45.194
What?

1622
01:51:46.260 --> 01:51:47.309
It's done.

1623
01:51:47.528 --> 01:51:50.151
So he went back to Quai Blériot,
the darling.

1624
01:51:50.343 --> 01:51:53.770
- No. He told the driver, Rue Turenne.
- What do you mean, Rue Turenne?

1625
01:51:53.772 --> 01:51:57.019
You see, you see! The poor thing didn't
seek refuge at her house.

1626
01:51:57.106 --> 01:52:01.074
He went to his mother's! His home. That
other place was never his home. Never!

1627
01:52:01.180 --> 01:52:04.624
- Children know who loves them. - Remain
seated. - He's waiting for me! - Sit down!

1628
01:52:04.720 --> 01:52:05.541
Brute!

1629
01:52:09.256 --> 01:52:12.386
It all comes down to
which one of you loves him more.

1630
01:52:12.841 --> 01:52:16.495
Which one of you tonight killed a
woman on Rue Jarente?

1631
01:52:17.360 --> 01:52:21.224
Which one of you committed a crime
similar to his, in the hopes of saving him?

1632
01:52:21.329 --> 01:52:22.413
Which one?

1633
01:52:23.347 --> 01:52:26.950
- That one tonight surpassed the other.
- I'd do anything for my son.

1634
01:52:27.177 --> 01:52:29.310
In any case, she gambled her head.

1635
01:52:29.703 --> 01:52:33.501
Maurin will keep his. They'll stick him
in an asylum, with his own bed, his toys...

1636
01:52:33.606 --> 01:52:34.852
He'll be thrilled.

1637
01:52:34.959 --> 01:52:38.744
But for 4 months, Paris has been
terrified. And jurors won't forgive that.

1638
01:52:38.849 --> 01:52:40.947
It's the woman who'll pay.

1639
01:52:41.200 --> 01:52:44.907
That one tonight made a supreme sacrifice
and loved him more than the other one.

1640
01:52:45.073 --> 01:52:49.007
- More than he can ever be loved.
- No one loves him like I do. No one!

1641
01:52:49.679 --> 01:52:53.272
- Is it you? - I don't care what he's done.
- Is it you? - I don't even care to know.

1642
01:52:53.342 --> 01:52:57.417
- Then say it! That's all I want to know!
Is it you? Eh, is it? - Yes! Yes! I did it.

1643
01:52:57.522 --> 01:53:00.896
I did it! I killed. He's my child.
I had the right, every right.

1644
01:53:07.779 --> 01:53:10.402
- Where did the crime take place?
- Rue Jarente.

1645
01:53:10.506 --> 01:53:13.060
- Yes, but where exactly?
- I don't remember.

1646
01:53:13.173 --> 01:53:15.516
What color was the victim's dress?

1647
01:53:16.215 --> 01:53:19.345
The dress was blue, with white stripes.

1648
01:53:24.799 --> 01:53:26.321
That's correct.

1649
01:53:32.325 --> 01:53:34.057
Lucas.
Come back in.

1650
01:53:35.596 --> 01:53:38.934
Take Mme Maurin's statement.
I have something else to do.

1651
01:53:41.864 --> 01:53:42.738
I hope

1652
01:53:42.739 --> 01:53:44.993
you won't retract your statement, eh?

1653
01:53:45.413 --> 01:53:47.196
Don't worry, Inspector.

1654
01:53:48.455 --> 01:53:50.116
I'm going all the way.

1655
01:54:51.517 --> 01:54:54.664
<i>Yet when the heart sings of romance</i>

1656
01:54:58.922 --> 01:55:02.051
<i>I forget all disappointments
and good sense</i>

1657
01:55:05.643 --> 01:55:08.774
<i>I always believe happiness is beginning</i>

1658
01:55:14.755 --> 01:55:16.277
M. Marcel!

1659
01:55:16.906 --> 01:55:18.934
What are you doing here?

1660
01:55:19.319 --> 01:55:20.595
Mauricette.

1661
01:55:20.979 --> 01:55:23.585
What's the matter with you, M. Marcel?

1662
01:55:33.998 --> 01:55:36.131
That way, they won't come in.

1663
01:55:44.321 --> 01:55:45.414
Help!

1664
01:55:45.571 --> 01:55:47.496
You don't want to?
Why?

1665
01:55:47.723 --> 01:55:49.837
Why don't you ever want to?

1666
01:55:51.701 --> 01:55:53.957
M. Marcel.
Leave me alone.

1667
01:55:53.958 --> 01:55:55.006
Be nice.

1668
01:55:56.142 --> 01:55:57.313
Slut.

1669
01:55:57.873 --> 01:55:59.954
M. Marcel, I beg you.

1670
01:56:00.460 --> 01:56:01.632
It's me.

1671
01:56:32.050 --> 01:56:33.589
Marcel, give me the knife.

1672
01:56:43.885 --> 01:56:45.931
You promised me you'd behave like a man.

1673
01:56:48.694 --> 01:56:50.669
But why don't they want to?

1674
01:56:50.823 --> 01:56:52.939
Come on, be reasonable. Give it.

1675
01:56:56.418 --> 01:56:57.467
Come on.

1676
01:57:01.348 --> 01:57:04.059
Marcel, I won't ask a second time.
Come on, give.

1677
01:57:06.191 --> 01:57:07.240
Give.

1678
01:57:13.538 --> 01:57:15.112
Don't make me yell.

1679
01:57:15.357 --> 01:57:16.458
Come on, give.

1680
01:57:16.930 --> 01:57:19.010
No, I don't want to.

1681
01:57:24.268 --> 01:57:26.034
Come on, be nice. Give.

1682
01:57:26.777 --> 01:57:28.070
Let's go. Give.

1683
01:57:28.875 --> 01:57:30.344
Let go of me!

1684
01:57:30.467 --> 01:57:31.813
Let me go.

1685
01:57:50.297 --> 01:57:52.902
Sir, what do we about the report?

1686
01:57:54.178 --> 01:57:55.753
Should I see Lucas?

1687
01:57:56.015 --> 01:57:57.851
You're not taking the car?

1688
01:57:58.331 --> 01:58:00.429
Ah, not a moment too soon.
